/-!
# Nef self-intersections, flipped curves, surface discrepancies and cyclic covers

Four results from Kollár–Mori's treatment of the minimal model program.

* **A lower bound for the self-intersection of a nef divisor.** Let `X` be a projective variety
  of dimension `n` over a field `k` and `D` a nef Cartier divisor. If `mD ∼ A + E` with `m > 0`,
  `A` very ample and `E` effective, then `(Aⁿ) ≤ mⁿ (Dⁿ)` (Kollár–Mori, Proposition 2.61). Write
  `Q = 𝒪_X(mD) ≅ 𝒪_X(A) ⊗ 𝒪_X(E)`. Multilinearity gives `(Qⁿ) = mⁿ (Dⁿ)` and, replacing the
  copies of `𝒪_X(A)` by copies of `Q` one slot at a time,
  `(Qⁿ) - (Aⁿ) = ∑ (Q^{i} · A^{n-1-i} · E)`. Each term is a mixed degree along the zero scheme
  of the canonical section of `𝒪_X(E)` ([Stacks, Tag 0BEU]), nonnegative because `Q` is nef and
  `𝒪_X(A)` is ample (Kollár–Mori, proof of Theorem 1.38).
* **Flipped curves cover the exceptional set.** If `f⁺ : X⁺ ⟶ Y` is a `(K + D)`-flip, every
  closed point of `Ex(f⁺)` lies on a flipped curve that `f⁺` contracts to a point: `f⁺` is
  proper birational onto the normal variety `Y`, so `f⁺_* 𝒪_{X⁺} = 𝒪_Y` (Kollár–Mori,
  Definition 3.33).
* **Numerical discrepancies are pair discrepancies.** On a resolution `f : Y ⟶ X` of a normal
  surface pair `(X, Δ)` over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, the solutions
  of `∑ᵢ aᵢ (Eᵢ · Eⱼ) = ((K_Y + f⁻¹_* Δ) · Eⱼ)` are the discrepancies `a(Eᵢ, X, Δ)`
  (Kollár–Mori, Notation 4.1, Definition 2.25). Writing `K_X = div ω` and `M = m(K_X + Δ)`
  Cartier, `div(f^*ω) + f⁻¹_* Δ = f^*M/m + ∑_E a(E, X, Δ) E`; intersecting with an exceptional
  curve kills `f^*M` by the projection formula, and the numerical equations have a unique
  solution.
* **General cyclic covers are normal.** Let `X` be a normal variety over an algebraically closed
  field of characteristic zero, `mM` Cartier, and `s₀, …, s_N` sections of `𝒪_X(mM)` spanning a
  basepoint-free system with nonempty general member. For general `c` the cyclic cover
  `Spec_X ⊕_{i<m} 𝒪_X(-iM)` of `(M, m, ∑ cᵢ sᵢ)` is a normal variety (Kollár–Mori, 5.19, 5.25).
  By Bertini the branch divisor is reduced, so at each prime divisor the local algebra is
  `R[w]/(wᵐ - u)` with `u` a unit or a uniformizer; in the first case integral elements are
  recovered from traces, in the second `wᵐ - u` is Eisenstein.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.sheafSelfIntersectionNumber_le_pow_mul_of_isNef`: `(Aⁿ) ≤ mⁿ (Dⁿ)`.
* `MMP.Mori.IsFlip.exists_isFlippedCurve_of_mem_exceptionalSet`: flipped curves cover `Ex(f⁺)`.
* `MMP.Mori.isNumericalDiscrepancy_iff_isDiscrepancy`: numerical discrepancies computed on a
  resolution of a surface are the discrepancies of the pair.
* `MMP.Mori.DivisorialCyclicCover.exists_dense_open_isNormalVariety_cover`: a general cyclic
  cover branched along a free linear system is a normal variety.

## Implementation notes

The intersection numbers of the first result are those of the invertible sheaves
`MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf D`, taken against `X` itself. The source cuts `X` by a
general member of `|A|` and inducts on the dimension, which needs a Bertini theorem; the
telescoping identity above uses only multilinearity, restriction to an effective divisor and
the nonnegativity of mixed degrees against an ample sheaf, and works over every field.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori]
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BEU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BEU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

/-! ## A lower bound for the self-intersection of a nef divisor -/

namespace MMP.Mori

section NefSelfIntersection

open Opposite

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.isInvertible_update

local notation "𝒪(" D ")" => MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf D

/-! ### Families with two values -/

section Families

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {d : ℕ}

/-- The family with `A` in the slots satisfying `p` and `B` in the others. -/
private def pick (p : Fin d → Prop) [DecidablePred p] (A B : X.Modules) : Fin d → X.Modules :=
  fun q => if p q then A else B

private theorem isInvertible_pick (p : Fin d → Prop) [DecidablePred p] (A B : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 A]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 B] (q : Fin d) :
    SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (pick p A B q) := by
  unfold pick; split_ifs <;> assumption

private theorem pick_empty (A B : X.Modules) :
    pick (· ∈ (∅ : Finset (Fin d))) A B = fun _ => B :=
  funext fun _ => by simp [pick]

private theorem pick_univ (A B : X.Modules) :
    pick (· ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin d))) A B = fun _ => A :=
  funext fun _ => by simp [pick]

private theorem pick_insert (S : Finset (Fin d)) (A B : X.Modules) (a : Fin d) :
    pick (· ∈ insert a S) A B = Function.update (pick (· ∈ S) A B) a A := by
  funext q
  by_cases h : q = a
  · subst h
    simp [pick]
  · simp [pick, h, Function.update_of_ne h]

private theorem update_pick_of_notMem {S : Finset (Fin d)} (A B : X.Modules) {a : Fin d}
    (ha : a ∉ S) : Function.update (pick (· ∈ S) A B) a B = pick (· ∈ S) A B := by
  funext q
  by_cases h : q = a
  · subst h
    simp [pick, ha]
  · simp [Function.update_of_ne h]

end Families

attribute [local instance] isInvertible_pick

/-! ### Multilinearity -/

section Multilinearity

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f]
  (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] (d : ℕ) (hd : topologicalKrullDim Z ≤ d)

/-- Additivity in one slot: if `Q ≅ A ⊗ B`, putting `Q` in slot `j` gives the sum of the
intersection numbers with `A` and with `B` in that slot. -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_update_of_iso_tensorObj (F : Fin d → X.Modules)
    [∀ q, SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (F q)] (j : Fin d)
    (Q A B : X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 Q]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 A]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 B]
    (e : Q ≅ Scheme.Modules.tensorObj A B) :
    intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update F j Q) =
      intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update F j A) +
        intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update F j B) := by
  simpa only [Function.update_idem] using intersectionNumber_update_tensor k f i d hd j
    (Function.update F j Q) A B (eqToIso (Function.update_self j _ F) ≪≫ e)

/-- Replacing `𝒪_X(D)` by `𝒪_X(mD)` in one slot multiplies the intersection number by `m`. -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_update_sheaf_nsmul (F : Fin d → X.Modules)
    [∀ q, SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (F q)]
    (j : Fin d) (D : X.CartierDivisor) (m : ℕ) :
    intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update F j 𝒪(m • D)) =
      m * intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update F j 𝒪(D)) := by
  induction m with
  | zero =>
    -- `𝒪_X(0) ≅ 𝒪_X(0) ⊗ 𝒪_X(0)`
    have := intersectionNumber_update_of_iso_tensorObj k f i d hd F j 𝒪(0) _ _
      (eqToIso (by rw [add_zero]) ≪≫ (MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sheafMulIso 0 0).symm)
    rw [zero_nsmul, Nat.cast_zero, zero_mul]
    omega
  | succ m ih =>
    rw [intersectionNumber_update_of_iso_tensorObj k f i d hd F j _ _ _
      (eqToIso (by rw [succ_nsmul]) ≪≫
        (MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sheafMulIso (m • D) D).symm), ih]
    push_cast
    ring

/-- `((mD)^d · Z) = m^d (D^d · Z)`. -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_sheaf_nsmul (D : X.CartierDivisor) (m : ℕ) :
    intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => 𝒪(m • D)) =
      (m : ℤ) ^ d * intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => 𝒪(D)) := by
  have key : ∀ S : Finset (Fin d), intersectionNumber k f i d hd (pick (· ∈ S) 𝒪(m • D) 𝒪(D)) =
      (m : ℤ) ^ S.card * intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => 𝒪(D)) := by
    intro S
    induction S using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty =>
      rw [Finset.card_empty, pow_zero, one_mul]
      exact intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_empty _ _)
    | insert a S ha ih =>
      rw [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_insert S _ _ a),
        intersectionNumber_update_sheaf_nsmul,
        intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (update_pick_of_notMem _ _ ha), ih,
        Finset.card_insert_of_notMem ha, pow_succ]
      ring
  simpa [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_univ _ _)] using key Finset.univ

/-- **Telescoping.** If `Q ≅ A ⊗ E`, then `(Q^d · Z) - (A^d · Z)` is the sum, over the steps of a
chain `∅ = S₀ ⊂ ⋯ ⊂ S_d = univ`, of the intersection numbers of the families with `Q` in the
slots of `S`, `E` in the new slot `a ∉ S` and `A` in the others. So `(A^d · Z) ≤ (Q^d · Z)` as
soon as each of these is nonnegative. -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_le_of_iso_tensorObj (Q A E : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 Q]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 A]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 E]
    (e : Q ≅ Scheme.Modules.tensorObj A E)
    (hnn : ∀ (S : Finset (Fin d)) (a : Fin d), a ∉ S →
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i d hd (Function.update (pick (· ∈ S) Q A) a E)) :
    intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => A) ≤ intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => Q) := by
  have key : ∀ S : Finset (Fin d), intersectionNumber k f i d hd (fun _ => A) ≤
      intersectionNumber k f i d hd (pick (· ∈ S) Q A) := by
    intro S
    induction S using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty => exact (intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_empty _ _)).ge
    | insert a S ha ih =>
      rw [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_insert S _ _ a),
        intersectionNumber_update_of_iso_tensorObj k f i d hd _ a Q A E e,
        intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (update_pick_of_notMem _ _ ha)]
      linarith [hnn S a ha]
  simpa [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hd (pick_univ _ _)] using key Finset.univ

end Multilinearity

/-! ### Mixed degrees against an ample sheaf -/

section Mixed

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible (tensorPower)

attribute [local instance] isInvertible_finCons

/-- An intersection number on a closed subscheme `Z` of dimension `d` is nonnegative as soon as
it is nonnegative on every integral closed subscheme of dimension `d`: it is a positive
combination of these over the top-dimensional components of `Z` ([Stacks, Tag 0BES]). -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_nonneg_of_forall_isIntegral (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f] (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (d : ℕ) (hd : topologicalKrullDim Z = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) (L : Fin d → X.Modules)
    [∀ j, SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (L j)]
    (hnn : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (j : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion j] [IsIntegral W]
      (hW : topologicalKrullDim W = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)), 0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f j d hW.le L) :
    0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i d hd.le L := by
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  haveI : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  haveI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  haveI : (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Z).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CurveEulerBridge.isCoherent_unit k (i ≫ f)
  haveI : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Z)).IsCoherent :=
    isCoherent_pushforward_of_isClosedImmersion i (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Z)
  haveI : Finite (TopDimIntegralSubscheme
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Z))) :=
    finite_topDimIntegralSubscheme k f _
  classical
  haveI : Fintype (TopDimIntegralSubscheme
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Z))) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  rw [intersectionNumber_eq_sum_topDimComponents k f i d hd L, finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype]
  refine Finset.sum_nonneg fun W _ => mul_nonneg (sheafMultiplicity_genericPt_pos k f _ W).le ?_
  haveI : IsIntegral W.1.subscheme := W.2.1
  exact hnn _ W.1.subschemeι (W.2.2.2.trans (by
    rw [Stacks.Chow.supp_pushforwardStructureSheaf i, topologicalKrullDim_range_eq i]
    exact hd))

/-- **Cutting by an ample sheaf.** Let `W` be an integral closed subscheme of dimension `d + 1`
and `M` ample. If the family `T` has nonnegative intersection number on every closed subscheme
of `W` of dimension `d`, then `(M · T · W) ≥ 0`: some power `M^n` restricts to `𝒪_W(D)` for an
effective Cartier divisor `D`, and `n (M · T · W) = (T · D)` ([Stacks, Tag 0BEU]). -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_cons_nonneg_of_isAmple (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X W : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f] (ι : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion ι]
    [IsIntegral W] {d : ℕ} (hW : topologicalKrullDim W = ((d + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (M : X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 M]
    (hM : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X M) (T : Fin d → X.Modules)
    [∀ q, SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (T q)]
    (hT : ∀ {Y : Scheme.{u}} (j : Y ⟶ W) [IsClosedImmersion j]
      (hY : topologicalKrullDim Y = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)),
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f (j ≫ ι) d hY.le T) :
    0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f ι (d + 1) hW.le (Fin.cons M T) := by
  have hMample : Scheme.Modules.IsAmple W ((Scheme.Modules.pullback ι).obj M) :=
    Stacks.PowerFamilyBridge.modulesIsAmple_of_isAmple _ _
      (Stacks.AmplePullbackCovering.isAmple_modulePullback_of_immersion_or_isEmbedding
        ι M hM (Or.inl ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩))
  obtain ⟨n, D, hn, hD, hDne, ⟨e⟩⟩ := exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_tensorPower_of_isAmple k
    (ι ≫ f) (by rw [hW]; exact_mod_cast d.succ_pos) _ hMample
  haveI : Nonempty D.subscheme := hDne
  haveI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D := hD
  have hDdim := topologicalKrullDim_subscheme_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor k (ι ≫ f) D hD hW
  haveI := isInvertible_finCons M T
  set G : Fin (d + 1) → X.Modules := Fin.cons M T
  set N := Function.update G 0 (tensorPower X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (G 0) (n : ℤ))
  haveI : ∀ q, SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 (N q) :=
    isInvertible_update G 0 _
  have hNiso : (Scheme.Modules.pullback ι).obj (N 0) ≅ Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf D :=
    eqToIso (congrArg (Scheme.Modules.pullback ι).obj (Function.update_self 0 _ G)) ≪≫
      Scheme.Modules.pullbackTensorPowerIso ι (G 0) n ≪≫ e
  have hNT : (fun t : Fin d => N t.succ) = T := funext fun t =>
    (Function.update_of_ne (Fin.succ_ne_zero t) _ _).trans (Fin.cons_succ _ _ _)
  refine nonneg_of_mul_nonneg_right ?_ (by exact_mod_cast hn : (0 : ℤ) < n)
  rw [← intersectionNumber_update_tensorPower k f ι (d + 1) hW.le G 0 n,
    intersectionNumber_eq_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor k f ι d hW.le N D hDdim.le hNiso,
    intersectionNumber_congr_family k f _ d _ hNT]
  exact hT D.subschemeι hDdim

/-- **Mixed degrees against an ample sheaf are nonnegative** (Kollár–Mori, proof of
Theorem 1.38, following [Stacks, Tag 0BEV]): if `(L^j · W) ≥ 0` for every integral closed `W` of
dimension `j` and `M` is ample, then every closed subscheme `Z` of dimension `j + s` has
`(L^j M^s · Z) ≥ 0`, the family being `M` in the `s` slots satisfying `lab` and `L` in the
others. -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_pick_nonneg_of_isAmple (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f] (L M : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 M]
    (hM : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X M) (j : ℕ)
    (hL : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (i : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral W]
      (hW : topologicalKrullDim W = (j : WithBot ℕ∞)),
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i j hW.le (fun _ => L)) :
    ∀ (s d : ℕ), d = j + s → ∀ {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
      (hdim : topologicalKrullDim Z = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) (lab : Fin d → Prop)
      [DecidablePred lab], (∑ q, if lab q then 1 else 0) = s →
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i d hdim.le (pick lab M L) := by
  classical
  intro s
  induction s with
  | zero =>
    intro d hdj Z i _ hdim lab _ hcnt
    obtain rfl : d = j := hdj
    have hfam : pick lab M L = fun _ => L := funext fun q => if_neg fun hq => by
      have : 0 < ∑ q, if lab q then 1 else 0 :=
        Finset.sum_pos' (fun _ _ => Nat.zero_le _) ⟨q, Finset.mem_univ _, by simp [hq]⟩
      omega
    rw [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i d hdim.le hfam]
    exact intersectionNumber_nonneg_of_forall_isIntegral k f i d hdim _ hL
  | succ s ih =>
    intro d hdj Z i _ hdim lab _ hcnt
    obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ : ∃ d', d = d' + 1 := ⟨j + s, by omega⟩
    obtain ⟨q0, hq0⟩ : ∃ q0, lab q0 := by
      by_contra h
      push Not at h
      simp [h] at hcnt
    -- move a slot holding `M` to the front
    rw [← intersectionNumber_comp_perm k f i (d + 1) hdim.le (pick lab M L) (Equiv.swap 0 q0)]
    have hcons : (fun q => pick lab M L (Equiv.swap 0 q0 q)) =
        Fin.cons M (pick (fun t : Fin d => lab (Equiv.swap 0 q0 t.succ)) M L) := by
      funext q
      refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun t => rfl) q
      simp [pick, hq0]
    refine le_of_le_of_eq ?_ (intersectionNumber_congr_family k f i (d + 1) hdim.le hcons).symm
    refine intersectionNumber_nonneg_of_forall_isIntegral k f i (d + 1) hdim _
      fun W ι _ _ hW => intersectionNumber_cons_nonneg_of_isAmple k f ι hW M hM _
        fun jY _ hY => ih d (by omega) (jY ≫ ι) hY _ ?_
    have := Equiv.sum_comp (Equiv.swap 0 q0) (fun q => if lab q then 1 else 0)
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_succ, Equiv.swap_apply_left, if_pos hq0] at this
    omega

end Mixed

/-! ### The step at the effective divisor -/

section Step

/-- **Each term of the telescoping sum is nonnegative.** Let `X` be integral of dimension
`d + 1`, proper over `k`, `L` invertible with `(L^j · W) ≥ 0` on every integral closed `W` of
dimension `j`, `M` ample, and `N` invertible with a nonzero global section. Then the
intersection number of the family with `N` in slot `a`, `L` in the slots of `S ∌ a` and `M`
in the others is nonnegative: it is a mixed degree of `L` and `M` on the zero scheme of the
section ([Stacks, Tag 0BEU]). -/
private theorem intersectionNumber_update_pick_nonneg (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f] [IsIntegral X] {d : ℕ}
    (hX : topologicalKrullDim X = ((d + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞)) (L M N : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 M]
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 N]
    (hM : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X M)
    (hL : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (i : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral W] {j : ℕ}
      (hW : topologicalKrullDim W = (j : WithBot ℕ∞)),
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i j hW.le (fun _ => L))
    (s : N.sections) (hs : s.eval (op ⊤) ≠ 0)
    (S : Finset (Fin (d + 1))) (a : Fin (d + 1)) (ha : a ∉ S) :
    0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f (𝟙 X) (d + 1) hX.le (Function.update (pick (· ∈ S) L M) a N) := by
  classical
  set G := Function.update (pick (· ∈ S) L M) a N with hG
  set σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin (d + 1)) := Equiv.swap 0 a with hσ
  rw [← intersectionNumber_comp_perm k f (𝟙 X) (d + 1) hX.le G σ]
  haveI : SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N :=
    ‹SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 N›
  have hreg := isRegularSection_of_eval_top_ne_zero N s hs
  haveI hDv : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X N (s.eval (op ⊤))) :=
    (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection X N s).2 hreg
  obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := (existsUnique_invertibleSheafIso_zeroScheme X N s hreg).exists
  set Dv := AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X N (s.eval (op ⊤))
  have h0 : G (σ 0) = N := by simp [hG, hσ]
  rw [intersectionNumber_eq_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor' k f (𝟙 X) d hX.le
    (fun j => G (σ j)) Dv ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackId X).app (G (σ 0)) ≪≫ eqToIso h0 ≪≫ e.symm)]
  -- the remaining family is a mixed family of `L` and `M`
  have hfam : (fun t : Fin d => G (σ t.succ)) = pick (fun t => σ t.succ ∉ S) M L := by
    funext t
    have hne : σ t.succ ≠ a := by
      rw [hσ, Ne, Equiv.swap_apply_eq_iff, Equiv.swap_apply_right]
      exact Fin.succ_ne_zero t
    simp only [hG, Function.update_of_ne hne, pick]
    split_ifs <;> simp_all
  rw [intersectionNumber_congr_family k f _ d _ hfam]
  by_cases hne : Nonempty Dv.subscheme
  · have hdim : topologicalKrullDim Dv.subscheme = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
      topologicalKrullDim_subscheme_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor k f Dv hDv hX
    set c := ∑ q : Fin d, if σ q.succ ∉ S then 1 else 0 with hc
    have hcd : c ≤ d := by
      calc c ≤ ∑ _q : Fin d, 1 := Finset.sum_le_sum fun q _ => by split_ifs <;> simp
        _ = d := by simp
    exact intersectionNumber_pick_nonneg_of_isAmple k f L M hM (d - c) (fun W i _ _ hW => hL W i hW)
      c d (by omega) (Dv.subschemeι ≫ 𝟙 X) hdim _ hc.symm
  · haveI : IsEmpty Dv.subscheme := not_nonempty_iff.mp hne
    haveI : IsEmpty (TopologicalSpace.IrreducibleCloseds Dv.subscheme) :=
      ⟨fun c => c.isIrreducible.nonempty.elim fun x _ => isEmptyElim x⟩
    rw [intersectionNumber_eq_zero_of_topologicalKrullDim_lt]
    rw [topologicalKrullDim, Order.krullDim_eq_bot]
    exact WithBot.bot_lt_coe _

end Step

/-! ### The inequality -/

section Main

/-- `𝒪_X(D₁) ≅ 𝒪_X(D₂)` for linearly equivalent Cartier divisors `D₁ ∼ D₂`. -/
private theorem nonempty_sheafIso_of_linearlyEquivalent {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {D₁ D₂ : X.CartierDivisor} (h : MMP.Intersection.LinearlyEquivalent D₁ D₂) :
    Nonempty (𝒪(D₁) ≅ 𝒪(D₂)) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := MMP.Intersection.mem_principalSubgroup_iff.mp h
  obtain rfl : D₁ = D₂ + MMP.Intersection.principalDivisor c := by rw [hc]; abel
  exact ⟨(MMP.CartierDivisor.sheafAddPrincipalIso D₂ c).symm⟩

/-- A very ample Cartier divisor has an ample invertible sheaf (in the sense of
`Stacks.Ample.IsAmple`). -/
private theorem isAmple_sheaf_of_isVeryAmple (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsProper (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] (A : X.CartierDivisor)
    (hA : MMP.Intersection.IsVeryAmple k (MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf A)) :
    Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X 𝒪(A) := by
  have h5 : ∃ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d ∧ Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.HasImmersionTwistOver
      (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) (Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule X 𝒪(A) (d : ℤ)) :=
    ⟨1, le_rfl, MMP.Resolution.Bridges.hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isVeryAmple k _ _ hA
      (Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModuleOneIso X 𝒪(A))⟩
  exact ((Stacks.AmpleRelativeFiniteType.tfae_six (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) 𝒪(A)).out 5 1).1 h5

/-- The canonical section of an effective Cartier divisor `E` on an integral scheme, read in
`𝒪_X(E)`, is a nonzero global section. -/
private theorem exists_sections_eval_ne_zero {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    (E : X.CartierDivisor) (hE : MMP.Intersection.IsEffective E) :
    ∃ s : 𝒪(E).sections, s.eval (op ⊤) ≠ 0 := by
  refine ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop 𝒪(E) (MMP.CartierDivisor.canonicalSection E hE),
    ?_⟩
  intro h0
  erw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop_eval_top] at h0
  have h1 := MMP.CartierDivisor.sectionVal_canonicalSection E hE
  have h2 : MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sectionVal
      ((0 : 𝒪(E).val.obj (op ⊤))) = 0 := rfl
  erw [h0, h2] at h1
  have h3 : (1 : Γ(X, ⊤)) = 0 := MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.toK_injective ⊤
    (by rw [map_one, map_zero]; exact h1.symm)
  exact one_ne_zero h3

/-- **Kollár–Mori, Proposition 2.61, (1) ⇒ (2), the key inequality.** Let `X` be a projective
variety of dimension `n` over `k`, `D` a nef Cartier divisor, `m > 0` an integer, `A` a very
ample and `E` an effective Cartier divisor with `mD ∼ A + E`. Then `(Aⁿ) ≤ mⁿ (Dⁿ)`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_nef_selfintersection_lower_bound"]
public theorem sheafSelfIntersectionNumber_le_pow_mul_of_isNef (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsProper (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hX : IsProjectiveVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) {n : ℕ} (hn : topologicalKrullDim X = n)
    (D A E : X.CartierDivisor)
    (hD : IsNef k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) (MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf D))
    {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) (hA : MMP.Intersection.IsVeryAmple k (MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf A))
    (hE : MMP.Intersection.IsEffective E)
    (hmD : MMP.Intersection.LinearlyEquivalent (m • D) (A + E)) :
    sheafSelfIntersectionNumber k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) (𝟙 X) n hn.le
        (MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf A) ≤
      (m : ℤ) ^ n * sheafSelfIntersectionNumber k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) (𝟙 X) n hn.le
        (MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf D) := by
  classical
  set f := X ↘ Spec (.of k)
  haveI : IsIntegral X := IsVariety.toIsIntegral f (self := hX.toIsVariety)
  unfold MMP.Mori.sheafSelfIntersectionNumber
  rw [MMP.Mori.Snapper.sheafIntersectionNumber_eq_intersectionNumber,
    MMP.Mori.Snapper.sheafIntersectionNumber_eq_intersectionNumber,
    ← intersectionNumber_sheaf_nsmul]
  -- `𝒪_X(mD) ≅ 𝒪_X(A) ⊗ 𝒪_X(E)`
  obtain ⟨e₁⟩ := nonempty_sheafIso_of_linearlyEquivalent hmD
  have hsplit : 𝒪(m • D) ≅ Scheme.Modules.tensorObj 𝒪(A) 𝒪(E) :=
    e₁ ≪≫ (MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sheafMulIso A E).symm
  -- the degrees of `𝒪_X(mD)` on integral closed subschemes are nonnegative (Kleiman)
  have hL : ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (i : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral W] {j : ℕ}
      (hW : topologicalKrullDim W = (j : WithBot ℕ∞)),
      0 ≤ intersectionNumber k f i j hW.le (fun _ => 𝒪(m • D)) := by
    intro W i _ _ j hW
    rw [intersectionNumber_sheaf_nsmul]
    have h := MMP.Mori.sheafSelfIntersectionNumber_nonneg_of_isNef k f hX _ hD W i hW
    unfold MMP.Mori.sheafSelfIntersectionNumber at h
    rw [MMP.Mori.Snapper.sheafIntersectionNumber_eq_intersectionNumber] at h
    exact mul_nonneg (pow_nonneg (Nat.cast_nonneg m) j) h
  have hM := isAmple_sheaf_of_isVeryAmple k A hA
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_sections_eval_ne_zero E hE
  -- telescoping: replace the copies of `𝒪_X(A)` by copies of `𝒪_X(mD)` one at a time
  refine intersectionNumber_le_of_iso_tensorObj k f (𝟙 X) n hn.le _ _ _ hsplit fun S a ha => ?_
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_one_of_ne_zero a.pos.ne'
  exact intersectionNumber_update_pick_nonneg k f hn _ _ _ hM hL s hs S a ha

end Main

end NefSelfIntersection

end MMP.Mori

/-! ## Flipped curves cover the exceptional set of a flip -/

namespace MMP.Mori

section FlippedCurves

/-- An irreducible closed curve `W ⊆ X⁺` contracted by the flip `f⁺` to a point, taken with its
reduced structure, is a flipped curve. -/
private lemma isFlippedCurve_vanishingIdeal {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y X' : Scheme.{u}}
    {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {sX' : X' ⟶ Spec (.of k)}
    [CompactSpace X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X']
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X'] [IsNormal X'] {K : Divisor X} {D : QDivisor X} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    {fp : X' ⟶ Y} (h : IsFlip sX sY sX' K D f fp) {W : Set X'} (hWc : IsClosed W)
    (hWi : IsIrreducible W) (hWd : topologicalKrullDim W = 1) (hW : (fp.base '' W).Subsingleton) :
    IsFlippedCurve sX sY sX' K D f fp (.vanishingIdeal ⟨W, hWc⟩) := by
  refine ⟨h, ⟨StacksTag09NX.isIntegral_subscheme_vanishingIdeal_of_isIrreducible _ hWi, ?_⟩, ?_⟩ <;>
    simp only [topologicalKrullDim_subscheme_eq, Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]
  · exact hWd
  · exact subset_exceptionalSet_of_subsingleton_image h.isNormalVariety.1
      h.isFlippingContraction.isNormalVariety_target.1 h.comp_eq h.isBirationalMorphism hWc hWi
      hWd hW

/-- **Flipped curves cover the exceptional set.** If `f⁺ : X⁺ ⟶ Y` is a `(K + D)`-flip of `f`,
every closed point `x ∈ Ex(f⁺)` lies on a flipped curve `C⁺` (`MMP.Mori.IsFlippedCurve`) with
`f⁺(C⁺)` a point. -/
@[mmp "lem_km3c_flipped_curves_cover_exceptional_set"]
public theorem IsFlip.exists_isFlippedCurve_of_mem_exceptionalSet {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X Y X' : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)}
    {sX' : X' ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [CompactSpace X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    [CompactSpace X'] [IsLocallyNoetherian X'] [IsNormal X']
    {K : Divisor X} {D : QDivisor X} {f : X ⟶ Y} {fp : X' ⟶ Y}
    (h : IsFlip sX sY sX' K D f fp) {x : X'} (hxc : IsClosed ({x} : Set X'))
    (hx : x ∈ (exceptionalSet fp : Set X')) :
    ∃ C : X'.IdealSheafData, IsFlippedCurve sX sY sX' K D f fp C ∧
      x ∈ (C.support : Set X') ∧ (fp.base '' (C.support : Set X')).Subsingleton := by
  have hX' := h.isNormalVariety.1
  have hY := h.isFlippingContraction.isNormalVariety_target
  have := h.isProper
  obtain ⟨W, hWc, hWi, hWd, hxW, y, hy⟩ :=
    exists_isIrreducible_curve_image_eq_singleton_of_mem_exceptionalSet hX' hY.1 fp h.comp_eq
      h.isBirationalMorphism
      (MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isIso_app_and_isConnected_of_isBirationalMorphism
        sX' sY hX' hY fp h.isBirationalMorphism).1 hxc hx
  have hW : (fp.base '' W).Subsingleton := hy ▸ Set.subsingleton_singleton
  exact ⟨_, isFlippedCurve_vanishingIdeal h hWc hWi hWd hW, by simpa, by simpa⟩

end FlippedCurves

end MMP.Mori

/-! ## Numerical discrepancies on a resolution of a surface -/

namespace MMP.Mori

section NumericalDiscrepancy

/-- In a quasi-compact scheme of dimension at most two, a point of coheight at least two is
closed. -/
private theorem isClosed_of_two_le_coheight {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X ≤ 2) {x : X} (hx : 2 ≤ Order.coheight x) :
    IsClosed ({x} : Set X) := by
  by_contra hcl
  obtain ⟨c, -, hxc, hne⟩ := exists_isClosed_singleton_specializes hcl
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hl⟩ := Order.exists_series_of_le_coheight x (n := 2) (by exact_mod_cast hx)
  let cl : X → TopologicalSpace.IrreducibleCloseds X := fun z =>
    ⟨closure {z}, isIrreducible_singleton.closure, isClosed_closure⟩
  have hlt : ∀ {z w : X}, z < w → cl z < cl w := by
    intro z w h
    have hsub : ∀ {z w : X}, z ≤ w → (closure {z} : Set X) ⊆ closure {w} := fun h =>
      closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
        (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp (Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mp h))) isClosed_closure
    refine lt_of_le_not_ge (hsub h.le) fun hle => h.2 ?_
    exact Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mpr (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr
      ((hle : (closure {w} : Set X) ⊆ closure {z}) (subset_closure rfl)))
  have hcx : c < x := lt_of_le_not_ge (Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mpr hxc)
    fun h => hne (hxc.antisymm (Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mp h)).eq
  have h0 : x < p ⟨1, by omega⟩ := by
    rw [← hp]
    exact p.step ⟨0, by omega⟩
  exact false_of_lt_lt_lt_of_topologicalKrullDim_le_two hdim (hlt hcx) (hlt h0)
    (hlt (p.step ⟨1, by omega⟩))

/-- On a resolution of a normal surface, a prime divisor is exceptional exactly when it is an
exceptional curve. -/
private theorem isExceptional_iff_isExceptionalCurve {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {f : Y ⟶ X}
    [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    (hX : IsNormalVariety k sX) (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 2)
    (hf : IsSmoothResolution sX f) (F : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y) :
    RationalMap.IsExceptional (X := Y) f.toRationalMap F ↔ IsExceptionalCurve f F.idealSheaf := by
  obtain ⟨hYv, hdimY, -⟩ := hf.isNormalVariety hX
  have : IsProper f := hf.isProper
  have : IsSeparated sX := hX.1.toIsSeparated
  have : IsSeparated (X ↘ Limits.terminal Scheme) := by
    rw [show (X ↘ Limits.terminal Scheme) = sX ≫ (Spec (.of k) ↘ Limits.terminal Scheme) from
      Limits.terminal.hom_ext _ _]
    infer_instance
  have : QuasiCompact sX := hX.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sX
  have : QuasiCompact (f ≫ sX) := hYv.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (f ≫ sX)
  have : IsIntegral Y := hf.isIntegral
  have : IsNoetherian Y := ⟨⟩
  rw [MMP.Positivity.isExceptional_toRationalMap_iff,
    MMP.Flips.le_closedsCodimension_iff_le_coheight]
  have hη : F.genericPoint ∈ (F.idealSheaf.support : Set Y) := by
    change F.genericPoint ∈ F.support
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
    exact subset_closure rfl
  have himg : f '' (F.idealSheaf.support : Set Y) ⊆ closure {f F.genericPoint} := by
    change f '' F.support ⊆ _
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
    have := image_closure_subset_closure_image (f := f) (s := {F.genericPoint}) f.continuous
    rwa [Set.image_singleton] at this
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h2 := h _ (subset_closure ⟨_, hη, rfl⟩)
    have hcl := isClosed_of_two_le_coheight (by rw [hdim]) h2
    refine ⟨⟨F.integral, ?_⟩, f F.genericPoint, ?_⟩
    · rw [topologicalKrullDim_subscheme_eq]
      have hηcl : ¬ IsClosed ({F.genericPoint} : Set Y) := by
        intro hc
        have := MMP.Threefold.Resolution.coheight_eq_two_of_isClosed hYv.1 (hdimY.trans hdim) hc
        rw [MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint] at this
        exact absurd this (by decide)
      obtain ⟨c, -, hηc, hne⟩ := exists_isClosed_singleton_specializes hηcl
      refine topologicalKrullDim_eq_one_of_ne_univ (by rw [hdimY, hdim])
        F.idealSheaf.support.isClosed ?_ hη ?_ hηc hne
      · intro huniv
        have hg : genericPoint Y ∈ (F.idealSheaf.support : Set Y) := huniv ▸ Set.mem_univ _
        change genericPoint Y ∈ F.support at hg
        rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure] at hg
        have heq : F.genericPoint = genericPoint Y :=
          (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hg).antisymm
            ((genericPoint_spec Y).specializes trivial) |>.eq
        have h1 := MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint F
        rw [heq, Order.coheight_eq_zero.mpr (fun b _ => Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mpr
          ((genericPoint_spec Y).specializes trivial))] at h1
        exact absurd h1 (by decide)
      · change c ∈ F.support
        rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
        exact specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp hηc
    · apply Set.Subset.antisymm
      · rwa [hcl.closure_eq] at himg
      · rintro _ rfl
        exact ⟨_, hη, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨-, x, hx⟩ y hy
    have hxcl : IsClosed ({x} : Set X) := by
      rw [← hx]
      exact f.isClosedMap _ F.idealSheaf.support.isClosed
    have hy' : y ∈ closure (f.base '' (F.idealSheaf.support : Set Y)) := hy
    rw [hx, hxcl.closure_eq] at hy'
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hy']
    exact (MMP.Threefold.Resolution.coheight_eq_two_of_isClosed hX.1 hdim hxcl).ge

/-- The pull-back of a nonzero rational pluricanonical form along a divisor over `X` is
nonzero. -/
private theorem pullbackRationalPluriForms_ne_zero {k : Type u} [Field k] [PerfectField k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsIntegral X] (hX : IsNormalVariety k sX) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : topologicalKrullDim X = n) (D : DivisorOver k sX) {m : ℤ}
    {τ : RationalPluriForms sX n m} (hτ : τ ≠ 0) :
    haveI := D.isIntegral
    haveI := D.isDominant
    pullbackRationalPluriForms sX D.f τ ≠ 0 := by
  let := functionFieldAlgebra sX
  have := D.isIntegral
  have := D.isDominant
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sX := hX.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  have hd := toNat_trdeg_functionField_of_topologicalKrullDim_eq (sX := sX) hn
  have hbij := D.isBirationalMorphism.functionFieldMap_bijective
  obtain ⟨ω, hω⟩ := exists_isPullbackGenerator_of_bijective sX D.f hbij hd
  let := functionFieldAlgebra (D.f ≫ sX)
  let := functionFieldMapAlgebra D.f
  have := isScalarTower_functionFieldMap sX D.f
  have hpull : pullbackRationalPluriForms sX D.f τ = pullbackFormsAlong hω m τ :=
    pullbackForms_eq hω m τ
  have hrepr := repr_pullbackFormsAlong hω m τ
  intro h0
  have h0' : pullbackFormsAlong hω m τ = 0 := hpull ▸ h0
  have h1 : algebraMap X.functionField D.Y.functionField
      ((ZTensorPower.basis (basisOfSpanSingleton hω.1 hω.ne_zero) m).repr τ ()) = 0 := by
    rw [← hrepr, h0']
    simp
  exact repr_ne_zero_of_ne_zero _ hτ ((map_eq_zero_iff _ (algebraMap _ _).injective).mp h1)

/-- **The discrepancy against a fixed form and a fixed Cartier multiple.** Let `K = div(ω)` and
`M = m(K + Δ)` a Cartier divisor with pull-back `M'` to `Y`. For a divisor `(Y, f, E)` over `X`
with `f` proper and discrepancy `a`, `a = ord_E(f^*ω) - coeff_E(M')/m`. -/
private theorem eq_ordPullback_sub_of_isDiscrepancy {k : Type u} [Field k] [PerfectField k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    {n : ℕ} {K : Divisor X} {Δ : QDivisor X} {D : DivisorOver k sX} {a : ℚ}
    (ha : IsDiscrepancy sX n K Δ D a) (hfp : IsProper D.f)
    {ω : RationalPluriForms sX n 1} (hω0 : ω ≠ 0) (hω : ∀ Γ, Γ.ordForm ω = K.coeff Γ)
    {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) {M : Divisor X}
    (hM : Divisor.toQDivisor M = (m : ℤ) • (Divisor.toQDivisor K + Δ)) (hMc : M.IsCartier)
    {M' : Divisor D.Y}
    (hM' : haveI := D.isLocallyNoetherian; haveI := D.isNormal; ∃ hC, M.IsPullback D.f hC M') :
    a = D.ordPullback ω - (m : ℚ)⁻¹ * M'.coeff D.E := by
  have hX := ha.1
  have hK := ha.2.1
  have hm0 : (m : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hm.ne'
  have hb : MMP.Intersection.IsLogDiscrepancy sX n (QDivisor.toRDivisor Δ) D
      (1 + (D.ordPullback ω : ℝ) - ∑ _i : Fin 1, (1 / (m : ℝ)) * (M'.coeff D.E : ℝ)) := by
    refine ⟨hX, hfp, ω, hω0, ⟨K, hK, fun Γ => (hω Γ).symm⟩, 1, fun _ => 1 / (m : ℝ),
      fun _ => M, fun _ => M', fun _ => hMc, fun Γ => ?_, fun _ => hM', rfl⟩
    have hMΓ : (M.coeff Γ : ℚ) = m * (K.coeff Γ + Δ.coeff Γ) := by
      have := congrArg (fun G : QDivisor X => G.coeff Γ) hM
      simp at this
      linear_combination this
    have hMΓ' : (M.coeff Γ : ℝ) = m * (K.coeff Γ + Δ.coeff Γ) := by exact_mod_cast hMΓ
    rw [QDivisor.coeff_toRDivisor, Fin.sum_univ_one, hMΓ', hω Γ]
    field_simp
  have h := MMP.Threefold.Bridges.eq_one_add_of_isDiscrepancy_of_isLogDiscrepancy ha hb
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_one, one_div] at h
  have h' : ((a : ℚ) : ℝ) = (((D.ordPullback ω : ℚ) - (m : ℚ)⁻¹ * (M'.coeff D.E : ℚ) : ℚ) : ℝ) := by
    push_cast
    linarith
  exact_mod_cast h'

/-- An exceptional curve `E` of `f : Y ⟶ X` whose subscheme is proper over `k` is a proper curve
of `Y`, with the generic point of `E`, contracted by `f`. -/
private theorem exists_properCurve_isContractedBy {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {f : Y ⟶ X} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    {E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (hE : IsExceptionalCurve f E.idealSheaf)
    (hp : IsProper (E.idealSheaf.subschemeι ≫ f ≫ sX)) :
    ∃ C : ProperCurve (f ≫ sX), C.point = E.genericPoint ∧ C.IsContractedBy f := by
  have hvan := vanishingIdeal_closure_genericPoint_eq_idealSheaf E
  have hcl : closure ({E.genericPoint} : Set Y) = E.support :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure E).symm
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hE.2
  have hfx : ∀ y ∈ E.support, f y = x := fun y hy =>
    Set.mem_singleton_iff.1 (hx ▸ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩)
  refine ⟨⟨E.genericPoint, ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩, rfl, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  · change topologicalKrullDim (Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal _).subscheme = 1
    rw [hvan]
    exact hE.1.2
  · change IsProper ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal _).subschemeι ≫ f ≫ sX)
    rw [hvan]
    exact hp
  · rw [← hcl] at hfx
    exact (hfx y hy).trans (hfx _ (subset_closure rfl)).symm

/-- **The projection formula on a contracted curve.** The pull-back `f^* M` of a Cartier divisor
`M` on a variety `X` meets every proper curve of `Y` contracted by `f` in `0`. -/
private theorem isIntersectionNumber_pullback_eq_zero {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {f : Y ⟶ X}
    [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    [QuasiCompact (f ≫ sX)] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [IsIntegral Y] [IsDominant f]
    [CompactSpace X] [CompactSpace Y] (hX : IsNormalVariety k sX) {M : Divisor X}
    (hMc : M.IsCartier) {C : ProperCurve (f ≫ sX)} (hC : C.IsContractedBy f)
    {E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (hCE : C.point = E.genericPoint) :
    IsIntersectionNumber (f ≫ sX)
      (Divisor.toQDivisor
        (M.pullback hMc (MMP.Threefold.Bridges.map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp f M)))
      E.idealSheaf 0 := by
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sX := hX.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  have : QuasiCompact sX := hX.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : IsSeparated sX := hX.1.toIsSeparated
  have hB := MMP.Threefold.Bridges.map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp f M
  have hM'c := hMc.isCartier_pullback f hB
  have h := isIntersectionNumber_of_properCurve _ (QDivisor.isQCartier_toQDivisor hM'c) C E hCE
  rwa [QDivisor.intersectionNumber_toQDivisor k _ _ _ _ hM'c,
    Divisor.degreeOn_pullback_eq_zero_of_isContractedBy f rfl hMc hB C hC, Int.cast_zero] at h

/-- **A decomposition of `K_Y + f⁻¹_* Δ` gives the numerical pull-back.** Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a
resolution of a normal surface, `K_Y` a canonical divisor of `Y` and `K' ∼ K_Y`. If
`K' + f⁻¹_* Δ = N + A`, where `N` meets every `f`-exceptional curve in `0` and `A` is supported on
the `f`-exceptional curves, then `A` solves the numerical pull-back equations of `(X, Δ)` on
`f`. -/
private theorem isNumericalPullbackSolution_of_eq_add {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {f : Y ⟶ X}
    [QuasiCompact (f ≫ sX)] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y]
    (hX : IsNormalVariety k sX) (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 2)
    (hf : IsSmoothResolution sX f) {KY K' : Divisor Y} (hKY : KY.IsCanonicalDivisor (f ≫ sX) 2)
    (hlin : KY.LinearlyEquivalent K') {Δ : QDivisor X} {N A : QDivisor Y}
    (hN : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y, IsExceptionalCurve f E.idealSheaf →
      IsIntersectionNumber (f ≫ sX) N E.idealSheaf 0)
    (hA : ∀ E ∈ A.support, IsExceptionalCurve f E.idealSheaf)
    (hsum : Divisor.toQDivisor K' + inverseTransformDivisor f Δ = N + A) :
    IsNumericalPullbackSolution sX f KY Δ A := by
  classical
  have hsm := hf.isSmoothScheme
  refine ⟨hf, ⟨2, hKY⟩, hA, fun Ej hEj => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a₀, ⟨-, -, -, h₀⟩, -⟩ := existsUnique_isNumericalPullbackSolution sX f hX hdim hf KY hKY Δ
  obtain ⟨-, b, -, ⟨hp, -, -, -⟩, -⟩ := h₀ Ej hEj
  obtain ⟨C, hCpt, -⟩ := exists_properCurve_isContractedBy hEj hp
  let I : QDivisor Y → ℚ := fun G => G.intersectionNumber k (f ≫ sX) C.ι C.dim_le
    (MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsm G)
  have hI : ∀ G, IsIntersectionNumber (f ≫ sX) G Ej.idealSheaf (I G) := fun G =>
    isIntersectionNumber_of_properCurve G _ C Ej hCpt
  refine ⟨fun Ei => I (Finsupp.single Ei 1),
    I (Divisor.toQDivisor KY + inverseTransformDivisor f Δ),
    fun Ei _ => hI _, hI _, ?_⟩
  have hK' := MMP.Flips.isIntersectionNumber_add_of_linearlyEquivalent hlin
    (hI (Divisor.toQDivisor KY + inverseTransformDivisor f Δ))
  rw [hsum] at hK'
  have hAI := isIntersectionNumber_sum A.support (D := fun Ei => A Ei • Finsupp.single Ei (1 : ℚ))
    (MMP.Flips.isIntersectionNumber_zero (hI 0))
    (fun Ei _ => (hI (Finsupp.single Ei 1)).smul (A Ei)
      (MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsm _))
  rw [show ∑ Ei ∈ A.support, A Ei • Finsupp.single Ei (1 : ℚ) = A by
    conv_rhs => rw [← Finsupp.sum_single A]
    simp [Finsupp.sum, Finsupp.smul_single_one]] at hAI
  simpa using (MMP.Flips.isIntersectionNumber_add (hN Ej hEj) hAI).unique hK'

/-- **Numerical discrepancies agree with pair discrepancies** (KM Notation 4.1, Definition 2.25).
Let `(X, Δ)` be a pair with `X` a normal surface over an algebraically closed field `k` of
characteristic zero, `K_X` a canonical divisor of `X`, `f : Y ⟶ X` a resolution, `K_Y` a canonical
divisor of `Y` and `E` an `f`-exceptional curve. Then `q ∈ ℚ` is the numerical discrepancy of `E`
computed on `f` if and only if it is the discrepancy `a(E, X, Δ)` of the pair. -/
@[mmp "lem_km4a_numerical_discrepancy_agrees"]
public theorem isNumericalDiscrepancy_iff_isDiscrepancy {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {f : Y ⟶ X}
    [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    [QuasiCompact (f ≫ sX)] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    {Δ : QDivisor X} (hP : IsPair sX Δ) (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 2)
    {KX : Divisor X} (hKX : KX.IsCanonicalDivisor sX 2)
    (hf : IsSmoothResolution sX f)
    {KY : Divisor Y} (hKY : KY.IsCanonicalDivisor (f ≫ sX) 2)
    {E : PrimeDivisor Y} (hE : IsExceptionalCurve f E.idealSheaf) (q : ℚ) :
    IsNumericalDiscrepancy sX f KY Δ E q ↔
      IsDiscrepancy sX 2 KX Δ
        ⟨Y, f, (hf.isNormalVariety hP.isNormalVariety).1, hf.isBirationalMorphism, E⟩ q := by
  classical
  have hX := hP.isNormalVariety
  obtain ⟨hYv, -, -⟩ := hf.isNormalVariety hX
  have : IsIntegral Y := hf.isIntegral
  have : IsProper f := hf.isProper
  have : QuasiCompact sX := hX.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sX
  have : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (f ≫ sX)
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (f ≫ sX) := hYv.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  let D : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y → DivisorOver k sX :=
    fun F => ⟨Y, f, hYv, hf.isBirationalMorphism, F⟩
  have : IsDominant f := (D E).isDominant
  -- the discrepancies `a(F) = ord_F(f^*ω) - coeff_F(M')/m` of the prime divisors of `Y`
  choose disc hdisc using fun F => MMP.Positivity.IsPair.exists_isDiscrepancy hP hKX (D F)
  obtain ⟨-, -, m, hm, ⟨M, hM, hMc⟩, -⟩ := hdisc E
  obtain ⟨ω, hω0, hω⟩ := MMP.Positivity.IsCanonicalDivisor.exists_ordForm_eq hX hKX
  have hB := MMP.Threefold.Bridges.map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp f M
  set M' : Divisor Y := M.pullback hMc hB
  set K'Y : Divisor Y := divisorOfForm (pullbackRationalPluriForms sX f ω)
  -- the crepant boundary `Δ_Y = M'/m - div(f^*ω)` and its exceptional part `A`
  set ΔY : QDivisor Y := (m : ℚ)⁻¹ • Divisor.toQDivisor M' - Divisor.toQDivisor K'Y
  have hΔYc : ∀ F, -ΔY.coeff F = disc F := fun F => by
    rw [eq_ordPullback_sub_of_isDiscrepancy (D := D F) (hdisc F) hf.isProper hω0 hω hm hM hMc
      ⟨hB, Divisor.isPullback_pullback hMc hB⟩]
    simp [ΔY, K'Y]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨hdec, -⟩ := IsCrepantBoundary.eq_inverseTransformDivisor_add_exceptional hP
    (ΔY := ΔY) fun F => hΔYc F ▸ hdisc F
  set A : QDivisor Y :=
    -Finsupp.filter (fun F => RationalMap.IsExceptional (X := Y) f.toRationalMap F) ΔY
  have hexc := isExceptional_iff_isExceptionalCurve (k := k) hX hdim hf
  have hAval : ∀ F, IsExceptionalCurve f F.idealSheaf → A F = disc F := fun F hF => by
    rw [← hΔYc F]
    simp [A, Finsupp.filter_apply, (hexc F).mpr hF]
    rfl
  -- `A` solves the numerical pull-back equations
  have hA : IsNumericalPullbackSolution sX f KY Δ A := by
    refine isNumericalPullbackSolution_of_eq_add hX hdim hf hKY
      (K' := K'Y) (N := (m : ℚ)⁻¹ • Divisor.toQDivisor M') ?_ (fun Ej hEj => ?_) (fun F hF => ?_) ?_
    · simpa using (MMP.Positivity.linearlyEquivalent_divisorOfForm_zsmul hYv hKY
        (pullbackRationalPluriForms_ne_zero hX (by rw [hdim]; rfl) (D E) hω0)).symm
    · obtain ⟨a₀, ⟨-, -, -, h₀⟩, -⟩ :=
        existsUnique_isNumericalPullbackSolution sX f hX hdim hf KY hKY Δ
      obtain ⟨-, b, -, ⟨hp, -, -, -⟩, -⟩ := h₀ Ej hEj
      obtain ⟨C, hCpt, hC⟩ := exists_properCurve_isContractedBy hEj hp
      simpa using (isIntersectionNumber_pullback_eq_zero hX hMc hC hCpt).smul (m : ℚ)⁻¹
        (MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hf.isSmoothScheme _)
    · by_contra h
      exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hF (by simp [A, Finsupp.filter_apply, (hexc F).not.mpr h])
    · rw [eq_sub_of_add_eq hdec.symm]
      simp only [A, ΔY]
      abel
  have huniq := existsUnique_isNumericalPullbackSolution sX f hX hdim hf KY hKY Δ
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨-, a, ha, rfl⟩
    rw [huniq.unique ha hA, hAval E hE]
    exact hdisc E
  · exact fun hq => ⟨hE, A, hA, by rw [hAval E hE]; exact IsDiscrepancy.eq (hdisc E) hq⟩

end NumericalDiscrepancy

end MMP.Mori

/-! ## General cyclic covers branched along a free linear system -/

namespace MMP.Mori.DivisorialCyclicCover

section CyclicCover

open TopologicalSpace Opposite Order MMP.Threefold.Bridges

section KummerAlgebra

open Polynomial
open Module in
private theorem trace_mem_range_of_subalgebra {R K E : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsPrincipalIdealRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] [CommRing E]
    [Algebra K E] [Algebra R E] [IsScalarTower R K E] [Module.Finite K E]
    (S : Subalgebra R E) [Module.Finite R S] (hS : Submodule.span K (S : Set E) = ⊤)
    (c : E) (hc : c ∈ S) :
    Algebra.trace K E c ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R K) := by
  have : NoZeroSMulDivisors R E := by
    refine ⟨fun {r x} h => ?_⟩
    rw [← algebraMap_smul K r x] at h
    rcases smul_eq_zero.mp h with h | h
    · exact Or.inl ((map_eq_zero_iff _ (IsFractionRing.injective R K)).mp h)
    · exact Or.inr h
  have : Module.Free R S := Module.free_of_finite_type_torsion_free'
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis R S
  haveI : Fintype (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R S) := inferInstance
  have hind : LinearIndependent K (fun i => ((b i : S) : E)) := by
    refine (LinearIndependent.iff_fractionRing (R := R) (K := K)).mp ?_
    exact b.linearIndependent.map' (Subalgebra.val S).toLinearMap
      (LinearMap.ker_eq_bot.mpr Subtype.val_injective)
  have hsum : ∀ s : S, ((s : S) : E) = ∑ i, b.repr s i • ((b i : S) : E) := fun s => by
    calc ((s : S) : E) = Subalgebra.val S (∑ i, b.repr s i • b i) := by rw [b.sum_repr]; rfl
      _ = _ := by rw [map_sum]; rfl
  have hspan : ⊤ ≤ Submodule.span K (Set.range fun i => ((b i : S) : E)) := by
    rw [← hS]
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr fun s hs => ?_
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe] at hs
    rw [show s = ((⟨s, hs⟩ : S) : E) from rfl, hsum]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ _
      (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  let b' : Basis (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R S) K E := Basis.mk hind hspan
  have hb' : ∀ i, b' i = ((b i : S) : E) := fun i => Basis.mk_apply _ _ i
  have hrepr : ∀ (s : S) i, b'.repr (s : E) i = algebraMap R K (b.repr s i) := by
    intro s i
    have : (s : E) = ∑ j, algebraMap R K (b.repr s j) • b' j := by
      rw [hsum s]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
      rw [algebraMap_smul, hb' j]
    rw [this, Basis.repr_sum_self]
  rw [Algebra.trace_eq_matrix_trace b']
  refine ⟨∑ i, b.repr ⟨c * ((b i : S) : E), S.mul_mem hc (b i).2⟩ i, ?_⟩
  rw [map_sum, Matrix.trace]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [Matrix.diag_apply, Algebra.leftMulMatrix_eq_repr_mul, hb']
  exact (hrepr ⟨c * ((b i : S) : E), S.mul_mem hc (b i).2⟩ i).symm

/-! ### The Kummer algebra over an abstract basis `1, w, …, wᵐ⁻¹` with `wᵐ = v` -/
namespace KummerBasis

section

variable {R K E : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K] [CommRing E] [Algebra K E]
  [Algebra R E] [IsScalarTower R K E] (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (v : R) (w : E)
  (hw : w ^ m = algebraMap R E v) (B : Module.Basis (Fin m) K E) (hB : ∀ i, B i = w ^ (i : ℕ))

include hw in
private theorem pow_eq (n : ℕ) :
    w ^ n = algebraMap K E (algebraMap R K (v ^ (n / m))) * w ^ (n % m) := by
  conv_lhs => rw [← Nat.div_add_mod n m]
  rw [pow_add, pow_mul, hw, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R K E, map_pow]

include hB in
private theorem repr_smul (c : K) (i j : Fin m) :
    B.repr (algebraMap K E c * B i) j = if i = j then c else 0 := by
  rw [← Algebra.smul_def, map_smul, Module.Basis.repr_self]
  simp [Finsupp.single_apply]

include hw hB in
private theorem repr_pow (n : ℕ) (j : Fin m) :
    B.repr (w ^ n) j = if (n % m : ℕ) = (j : ℕ) then algebraMap R K (v ^ (n / m)) else 0 := by
  have hlt : n % m < m := Nat.mod_lt _ (NeZero.pos m)
  have : w ^ (n % m) = B ⟨n % m, hlt⟩ := (hB ⟨n % m, hlt⟩).symm
  rw [pow_eq (K := K) m v w hw, this, repr_smul m w B hB]
  simp [Fin.ext_iff]

include hw hB in
private theorem trace_pow_lt (k : ℕ) (hk : k < m) :
    Algebra.trace K E (w ^ k) = if k = 0 then (m : K) else 0 := by
  classical
  rw [Algebra.trace_eq_matrix_trace B, Matrix.trace]
  have hj : ∀ j : Fin m, Matrix.diag (Algebra.leftMulMatrix B (w ^ k)) j =
      if k = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
    intro j
    rw [Matrix.diag_apply, Algebra.leftMulMatrix_eq_repr_mul, hB, ← pow_add, repr_pow m v w hw B hB]
    have hjm : (j : ℕ) < m := j.2
    by_cases hk0 : k = 0
    · subst hk0
      simp [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hjm, Nat.div_eq_of_lt hjm]
    · rw [if_neg hk0, if_neg]
      intro h
      by_cases hc : k + j < m
      · rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hc] at h
        omega
      · have : (k + j) % m = k + j - m := by
          rw [Nat.mod_eq_sub_mod (not_lt.mp hc), Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega)]
        omega
  simp only [hj]
  by_cases hk0 : k = 0 <;> simp [hk0]

include hw hB in
private theorem trace_pow (n : ℕ) :
    Algebra.trace K E (w ^ n) =
      if n % m = 0 then (m : K) * algebraMap R K (v ^ (n / m)) else 0 := by
  rw [pow_eq (K := K) m v w hw, ← Algebra.smul_def, map_smul, trace_pow_lt m v w hw B hB _
      (Nat.mod_lt _ (NeZero.pos m))]
  by_cases h : n % m = 0
  · simp [h, mul_comm]
  · simp [h]

end

variable {R K E : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsPrincipalIdealRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K]
  [IsFractionRing R K] [CommRing E] [Algebra K E] [Algebra R E] [IsScalarTower R K E]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m]

private theorem add_sub_mod_mod_eq_zero_iff {n i j k : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) (hi : i < n) (hj : j < n)
    (hk : k = (n - j) % n) : (i + k) % n = 0 ↔ i = j := by
  by_cases hj0 : j = 0
  · have : k = 0 := by simp [hk, hj0, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hn]
    rw [this, add_zero, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hi]
    omega
  · have : k = n - j := by rw [hk, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega)]
    constructor
    · intro h
      by_cases hc : i + k < n
      · rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hc] at h
        omega
      · rw [Nat.mod_eq_sub_mod (not_lt.mp hc), Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega)] at h
        omega
    · intro h
      rw [h, this, show j + (n - j) = n by omega, Nat.mod_self]

/-- **The coordinates of an integral element** of the Kummer algebra over a PID. -/
private theorem coords_mem (hm : IsUnit (m : R)) (v : R) (hv : IsUnit v) (w : E)
    (hw : w ^ m = algebraMap R E v) (B : Module.Basis (Fin m) K E) (hB : ∀ i, B i = w ^ (i : ℕ))
    (b : E) (hb : IsIntegral R b) (j : Fin m) :
    ∃ r : R, B.repr b j = algebraMap R K r := by
  classical
  have hwI : IsIntegral R w := by
    refine ⟨Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C v, monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m), ?_⟩
    rw [Polynomial.eval₂_sub, Polynomial.eval₂_X_pow, Polynomial.eval₂_C, hw, sub_self]
  let S : Subalgebra R E := Algebra.adjoin R {b, w}
  have : Module.Finite R S := Algebra.finite_adjoin_of_finite_of_isIntegral
    (Set.toFinite _) (by
      rintro x (rfl | rfl)
      exacts [hb, hwI])
  have : Module.Finite K E := Module.Finite.of_basis B
  have hS : Submodule.span K (S : Set E) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.mpr ?_
    rw [← B.span_eq]
    refine Submodule.span_mono ?_
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    rw [hB]
    exact S.pow_mem (Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inr rfl)) _
  have hjm : (j : ℕ) < m := j.2
  set k : ℕ := (m - j) % m with hk
  have hbk : b * w ^ k ∈ S := S.mul_mem (Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inl rfl))
    (S.pow_mem (Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inr rfl)) _)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := trace_mem_range_of_subalgebra (R := R) (K := K) (E := E) S hS _ hbk
  have hsum : b * w ^ k = ∑ i, B.repr b i • w ^ ((i : ℕ) + k) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← B.sum_repr b]
    rw [Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [smul_mul_assoc, hB, pow_add]
  have hkm : k < m := Nat.mod_lt _ (NeZero.pos m)
  have hcond : ∀ i : ℕ, i < m → ((i + k) % m = 0 ↔ i = j) := fun i hi =>
    add_sub_mod_mod_eq_zero_iff (NeZero.pos m) hi hjm hk
  have htr : Algebra.trace K E (b * w ^ k) =
      B.repr b j * ((m : K) * algebraMap R K v ^ (if (j : ℕ) = 0 then 0 else 1)) := by
    rw [hsum, map_sum]
    simp_rw [map_smul, trace_pow m v w hw B hB, smul_eq_mul]
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single j]
    · congr 1
      rw [if_pos ((hcond j hjm).mpr rfl)]
      by_cases hj0 : (j : ℕ) = 0
      · have : k = 0 := by simp [hk, hj0, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (NeZero.pos m)]
        rw [if_pos hj0, this, hj0]
        simp
      · have : k = m - j := by rw [hk, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (by omega)]
        rw [if_neg hj0, this, show (j : ℕ) + (m - j) = m by omega, Nat.div_self (NeZero.pos m)]
        simp
    · intro i _ hij
      have hi : (i : ℕ) < m := i.2
      rw [if_neg (fun h => hij (Fin.ext ((hcond i hi).mp h))), mul_zero]
    · simp
  rw [htr] at hr
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ'⟩ := hm.mul (hv.pow (if (j : ℕ) = 0 then 0 else 1))
  refine ⟨r * ↑μ⁻¹, ?_⟩
  have h2 : B.repr b j * algebraMap R K ((m : R) * v ^ (if (j : ℕ) = 0 then 0 else 1))
      = algebraMap R K r := by
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, map_natCast]
    exact hr.symm
  rw [← hμ'] at h2
  calc B.repr b j = B.repr b j * algebraMap R K (↑μ * ↑μ⁻¹) := by
        rw [Units.mul_inv, map_one, mul_one]
    _ = _ := by rw [map_mul, ← mul_assoc, h2, map_mul]

/-- Coordinates of an element of `R[w]` in the basis `1, w, …, w^{m-1}` lie in `R`. -/
private theorem repr_mem_of_mem_adjoin {R K E : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K]
    [CommRing E] [Algebra K E] [Algebra R E] [IsScalarTower R K E] (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (v : R)
    (w : E) (hw : w ^ m = algebraMap R E v) (B : Module.Basis (Fin m) K E)
    (hB : ∀ i, B i = w ^ (i : ℕ)) {b : E} (hb : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin R {w}) (j : Fin m) :
    ∃ r : R, B.repr b j = algebraMap R K r := by
  classical
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval] at hb
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hb
  rw [← hp]
  change ∃ r : R, B.repr (aeval w p) j = _
  rw [aeval_eq_sum_range]
  refine ⟨∑ i ∈ Finset.range (p.natDegree + 1),
    p.coeff i * (if (i % m : ℕ) = (j : ℕ) then v ^ (i / m) else 0), ?_⟩
  rw [map_sum, map_sum, Finset.sum_apply']
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [← algebraMap_smul K (p.coeff i), map_smul, Finsupp.smul_apply,
    repr_pow m v w hw B hB, smul_eq_mul, map_mul]
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- `Xᵐ - v` is Eisenstein at `(v)` for an irreducible `v` of a domain. -/
private theorem isEisensteinAt_X_pow_sub_C {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] {v : R}
    (hv : Irreducible v) (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] :
    (Polynomial.X ^ m - C v : R[X]).IsEisensteinAt (Ideal.span {v}) := by
  refine ⟨?_, fun {n} hn => ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [(monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m)).leadingCoeff, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    exact fun h => hv.not_isUnit (isUnit_of_dvd_one h)
  · rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    rw [natDegree_X_pow_sub_C] at hn
    rw [coeff_sub, coeff_X_pow, coeff_C, if_neg (by omega)]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  · rw [coeff_sub, coeff_X_pow, coeff_C, if_neg (NeZero.ne m).symm, if_pos rfl, zero_sub,
      Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    rintro ⟨c, hc⟩
    have : v * (1 + v * c) = 0 := by linear_combination -hc
    rcases mul_eq_zero.mp this with h | h
    · exact hv.ne_zero h
    · exact hv.not_isUnit (IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one (-c) (by linear_combination -h))

/-- **Integral elements of an Eisenstein Kummer extension.** Over a discrete valuation ring `R`
with fraction field `K`, if `E = K(w)` is a field with basis `1, w, …, w^{m-1}` and `w^m = v` is a
uniformizer, every element of `E` integral over `R` has its coordinates in `R`. -/
private theorem coords_mem_of_irreducible {R K E : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] [Field E]
    [Algebra K E] [Algebra R E] [IsScalarTower R K E] (m : ℕ) [NeZero m]
    (v : R) (hv : Irreducible v) (w : E)
    (hw : w ^ m = algebraMap R E v) (B : Module.Basis (Fin m) K E) (hB : ∀ i, B i = w ^ (i : ℕ))
    (b : E) (hb : IsIntegral R b) (j : Fin m) :
    ∃ r : R, B.repr b j = algebraMap R K r := by
  classical
  have hwI : IsIntegral R w := by
    refine ⟨Polynomial.X ^ m - C v, monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m), ?_⟩
    rw [eval₂_sub, eval₂_X_pow, eval₂_C, hw, sub_self]
  let PB : PowerBasis K E := ⟨w, m, B, hB⟩
  have hPBgen : PB.gen = w := rfl
  have hmK : minpoly K w = Polynomial.X ^ m - C (algebraMap R K v) := by
    have hdvd : minpoly K w ∣ Polynomial.X ^ m - C (algebraMap R K v) := minpoly.dvd _ _ (by
      rw [map_sub, map_pow, aeval_X, aeval_C, hw, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R K E, sub_self])
    refine (eq_of_monic_of_dvd_of_natDegree_le (minpoly.monic (hPBgen ▸ PB.isIntegral_gen))
      (monic_X_pow_sub_C _ (NeZero.ne m)) hdvd ?_).symm
    rw [natDegree_X_pow_sub_C, ← hPBgen, PB.natDegree_minpoly]
  have hmR : minpoly R w = Polynomial.X ^ m - C v := by
    apply map_injective (algebraMap R K) (IsFractionRing.injective R K)
    rw [← minpoly.isIntegrallyClosed_eq_field_fractions' K hwI, hmK]
    simp
  have hp : Prime v := hv.prime
  have hei : (minpoly R PB.gen).IsEisensteinAt (Submodule.span R {v}) := by
    rw [hPBgen, hmR]
    exact isEisensteinAt_X_pow_sub_C hv m
  -- clear denominators of the coordinates
  have hden : ∀ i : Fin m, ∃ d : R, d ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ a : R, algebraMap R K d * B.repr b i =
      algebraMap R K a := fun i => by
    obtain ⟨⟨a, d⟩, h⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (nonZeroDivisors R) (B.repr b i)
    exact ⟨d, nonZeroDivisors.coe_ne_zero d, a, by rw [mul_comm]; exact h⟩
  choose d hd0 a ha using hden
  obtain ⟨n, u, hu⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible
    (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ => hd0 i : ∏ i, d i ≠ 0) hv
  have hsm : v ^ n • b ∈ Algebra.adjoin R ({PB.gen} : Set E) := by
    rw [← B.sum_repr b, Finset.smul_sum]
    refine Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    have hc : ∃ r : R, algebraMap R K (v ^ n) * B.repr b i = algebraMap R K r := by
      refine ⟨(↑u⁻¹ : R) * ((∏ k ∈ Finset.univ.erase i, d k) * a i), ?_⟩
      have h1 : v ^ n = (↑u⁻¹ : R) * ∏ k, d k := by
        rw [hu, ← mul_assoc, Units.inv_mul, one_mul]
      rw [h1, ← Finset.mul_prod_erase _ _ (Finset.mem_univ i), map_mul, map_mul, map_mul,
        map_mul, ← ha i]
      ring
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hc
    have heq : v ^ n • (B.repr b i • B i) = r • w ^ (i : ℕ) := by
      rw [hB, ← algebraMap_smul K r, ← hr, mul_smul, algebraMap_smul]
    have hw' : w ∈ Algebra.adjoin R ({PB.gen} : Set E) :=
      Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mpr hPBgen.symm)
    rw [heq]
    exact Subalgebra.smul_mem _ (Subalgebra.pow_mem _ hw' _) r
  have hmem := mem_adjoin_of_smul_prime_pow_smul_of_minpoly_isEisensteinAt hp
    (hPBgen ▸ hwI) hb hsm hei
  exact repr_mem_of_mem_adjoin m v w hw B hB hmem j

end KummerBasis

end KummerAlgebra

section Coherence

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

private theorem primeDivisor_genericPoint_ne (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    E.genericPoint ≠ genericPoint X := by
  intro h
  have := E.coheight_genericPoint
  rw [h] at this
  have h0 : coheight (genericPoint X) = 0 := by
    rw [Order.coheight_eq_zero]
    intro b _
    exact ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes (Set.mem_univ b)).ge
  simp [h0] at this

private theorem exists_section_vanishing {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    ∃ a : Γ(X, U), genericPoint X ∈ X.basicOpen a ∧
      (E.genericPoint ∈ U → E.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen a) := by
  by_cases hE : E.genericPoint ∈ U
  · let V : X.Opens := U ⊓ ⟨(closure {E.genericPoint})ᶜ, isClosed_closure.isOpen_compl⟩
    have hηV : genericPoint X ∈ V := by
      refine ⟨hηU, fun hc => primeDivisor_genericPoint_ne E ?_⟩
      exact (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hc).antisymm
        ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes (Set.mem_univ _)) |>.eq
    obtain ⟨f, hfV, hηf⟩ := hU.exists_basicOpen_le ⟨_, hηV⟩ hηU
    exact ⟨f, hηf, fun _ hEf => (hfV hEf).2 (subset_closure rfl)⟩
  · exact ⟨1, by rwa [Scheme.basicOpen_one], fun h => absurd h hE⟩

/-- A regular function on an affine open `U ∋ η` that is invertible at the generic point and
vanishes at the generic point of each of finitely many prime divisors meeting `U`. -/
private theorem exists_section_vanishing_finset {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) (S : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) :
    ∃ a : Γ(X, U), genericPoint X ∈ X.basicOpen a ∧
      ∀ E ∈ S, E.genericPoint ∈ U → E.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen a := by
  classical
  choose g hgη hgE using exists_section_vanishing hU hηU
  refine ⟨∏ E ∈ S, g E, ?_, fun E hE hEU hEa => ?_⟩
  · induction S using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty => rwa [Finset.prod_empty, Scheme.basicOpen_one]
    | insert E s hE ih => rw [Finset.prod_insert hE, Scheme.basicOpen_mul]; exact ⟨hgη E, ih⟩
  · rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase _ _ hE, Scheme.basicOpen_mul] at hEa
    exact hgE E hEU hEa.1

/-- **Divisorial sheaves are coherent**: on an integral locally Noetherian normal scheme, the
sections of `𝒪_X(D)` over an affine open `U` form a finite `Γ(X, U)`-module. -/
private theorem finite_divisorialSubmodule [CompactSpace X] (D : Divisor X) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) : Module.Finite Γ(X, U) (D.divisorialSubmodule U) := by
  classical
  have := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  by_cases hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U
  swap
  · have : IsEmpty {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U} :=
      ⟨fun Z => hηU (MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint Z.1 ▸ Z.2)⟩
    have : Subsingleton (D.divisorialSubmodule U) :=
      ⟨fun _ _ => Subtype.ext <| funext isEmptyElim⟩
    exact Module.Finite.of_finite
  obtain ⟨a, hηa, hEa⟩ := exists_section_vanishing_finset hU hηU D.support
  let N : ℕ := D.support.sup fun E => (D.coeff E).toNat
  -- multiplication by `a ^ N` maps `𝒪_X(D)(U)` into `𝒪_X(0)(U)`
  have hmem : ∀ φ : D.divisorialSubmodule U,
      (0 : Divisor X).IsDivisorialSection U (a ^ N • φ.1) := by
    intro φ E hEU
    have hηE := E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU
    have hEgU := E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU
    have hgerm : X.presheaf.germ U _ hηE a = E.toComponent.hom (X.presheaf.germ U _ hEgU a) :=
      (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply X.presheaf hEgU
        E.specializes_genericPoint a).symm
    have h0 : (0 : Divisor X).coeff E = 0 := rfl
    rw [rationalFunctions_smul_apply, map_pow, hgerm, h0, neg_zero]
    by_cases hc : 0 < D.coeff E
    · have hE : E ∈ D.support := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr hc.ne'
      have hmax : X.presheaf.germ U _ hEgU a ∈
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk E.genericPoint) := fun hunit =>
        hEa E hE hEgU ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen X a _ hEgU).mpr hunit)
      refine (((E.ordGE_one_toComponent hmax).pow N).mul (φ.2 E hEU)).mono ?_
      have hN : (D.coeff E).toNat ≤ N :=
        Finset.le_sup (f := fun E => (D.coeff E).toNat) hE
      have := Int.toNat_of_nonneg hc.le
      omega
    · rw [← map_pow]
      exact ((φ.2 E hEU).toComponent_mul _).mono (by omega)
  let L : D.divisorialSubmodule U →ₗ[Γ(X, U)] (0 : Divisor X).divisorialSubmodule U :=
    { toFun := fun φ => ⟨a ^ N • φ.1, hmem φ⟩
      map_add' := fun φ ψ => Subtype.ext (smul_add _ _ _)
      map_smul' := fun r φ => Subtype.ext (smul_comm _ _ _) }
  have hL : Function.Injective L := by
    intro φ ψ h
    refine Subtype.ext (funext fun Z => ?_)
    have h1 := congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val h) Z
    change (a ^ N • φ.1) Z = (a ^ N • ψ.1) Z at h1
    rw [rationalFunctions_smul_apply, rationalFunctions_smul_apply] at h1
    have hu : IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ U _ Z.2 (a ^ N)) := by
      rw [map_pow]
      exact ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen X a _ Z.2).mp
        (by rw [MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint]; exact hηa)).pow N
    exact hu.mul_left_cancel h1
  -- `𝒪_X(0)(U)` is a quotient of `Γ(X, U)`
  let one : (0 : Divisor X).divisorialSubmodule U :=
    ⟨1, Divisor.IsDivisorialSection.one le_rfl U⟩
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton Γ(X, U) _ one) := by
    intro φ
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := Divisor.IsDivisorialSection.exists_eq φ.2
    refine ⟨s, Subtype.ext (funext fun Z => ?_)⟩
    change X.presheaf.germ U _ Z.2 s * 1 = φ.1 Z
    rw [mul_one, ← hs]
    rfl
  have := isNoetherian_of_surjective _ (LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr hsurj)
  have := isNoetherian_of_injective L hL
  infer_instance

end Coherence

section GenericFibre

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

/-- Every divisorial sheaf has a nonzero regular section on an affine open containing the generic
point: a power of a function vanishing along the relevant prime divisors. -/
private theorem exists_regular_divisorialSection (M : Divisor X) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    ∃ a : Γ(X, U), genericPoint X ∈ X.basicOpen a ∧
      M.IsDivisorialSection U ((toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op U) a) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨a, hηa, hEa⟩ := exists_section_vanishing_finset hU hηU M.support
  let N : ℕ := M.support.sup fun E => (M.coeff E).natAbs
  refine ⟨a ^ (N + 1), ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Scheme.basicOpen_pow _ _ (Nat.succ_pos N)]
    exact hηa
  · intro E hEU
    have hηE := E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU
    have hEgU := E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU
    have hgerm : X.presheaf.germ U _ hηE (a ^ (N + 1)) =
        E.toComponent.hom (X.presheaf.germ U _ hEgU (a ^ (N + 1))) :=
      (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply X.presheaf hEgU
        E.specializes_genericPoint _).symm
    change E.OrdGE (-M.coeff E) (X.presheaf.germ U _ hηE (a ^ (N + 1)))
    rw [hgerm]
    by_cases hc : M.coeff E < 0
    · have hE : E ∈ M.support := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr hc.ne
      have hmax : X.presheaf.germ U _ hEgU a ∈
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk E.genericPoint) := fun hunit =>
        hEa E hE hEgU ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen X a _ hEgU).mpr hunit)
      have hN : (M.coeff E).natAbs ≤ N :=
        Finset.le_sup (f := fun E => (M.coeff E).natAbs) hE
      rw [map_pow, map_pow]
      refine ((E.ordGE_one_toComponent hmax).pow (N + 1)).mono ?_
      push_cast
      omega
    · have h1 : E.OrdGE 0 (1 : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)) :=
        Or.inr (by simp)
      have := h1.toComponent_mul (X.presheaf.germ U _ hEgU (a ^ (N + 1)))
      rw [mul_one] at this
      exact this.mono (by omega)

end GenericFibre

section Fibre

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

/-- The unique irreducible component of an integral scheme. -/
private noncomputable def theComponent (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X] : irreducibleComponents X :=
  ⟨Set.univ, by simp [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]⟩

private theorem eq_theComponent (Z : irreducibleComponents X) : Z = theComponent X := by
  have h' := Z.2
  simp only [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at h'
  exact Subtype.ext h'

private theorem componentGenericPoint_mem {U : X.Opens} (hU : genericPoint X ∈ U)
    (Z : irreducibleComponents X) : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U := by
  rw [MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint Z]
  exact hU

@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def uniqueComponent {U : X.Opens} (hU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    Unique {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U} where
  default := ⟨theComponent X, componentGenericPoint_mem hU _⟩
  uniq Z := Subtype.ext (eq_theComponent Z.1)

/-- The germ at the generic point makes the stalk the fraction field of the sections over an
affine open. -/
private theorem isFractionRing_germ {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X}
    (hx : x = genericPoint X) (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    letI : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom.toAlgebra
    IsFractionRing Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  subst hx
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨_, hxU⟩⟩
  exact functionField_isFractionRing_of_isAffineOpen X U hU

/-- The sections of `𝒦_X` over an affine open containing the generic point form the fraction
field of the sections of `𝒪_X`. -/
private theorem isFractionRing_rationalFunctions {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    IsFractionRing Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) := by
  letI := uniqueComponent hηU
  have hZ := componentGenericPoint_mem hηU (theComponent X)
  letI : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X (theComponent X))) :=
    (X.presheaf.germ U _ hZ).hom.toAlgebra
  have := isFractionRing_germ hU (MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint (theComponent X)) hZ
  let e : ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) ≃ₐ[Γ(X, U)]
      X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X (theComponent X)) :=
    AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := RingEquiv.piUnique (R := fun Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X //
      componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U} => X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z.1)))
      (fun r => rfl)
  exact IsFractionRing.of_algEquiv e.symm

end Fibre

section Ambient

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ)

/-- `𝓛(U)` is a `𝒦_X(U)`-algebra. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def ambientAlgebraK (U : X.Opens) :
    Algebra ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) :=
  ((ofRationalFunctions m φ).app (op U)).hom.toAlgebra

/-- `𝓛(U)` is a `Γ(X, U)`-algebra. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def ambientAlgebraR (U : X.Opens) :
    Algebra Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) :=
  ((structureMap m φ).app (op U)).hom.toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] ambientAlgebraK ambientAlgebraR

private theorem isScalarTower_ambient (U : X.Opens) :
    IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U))
      ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl

attribute [local instance] isScalarTower_ambient

private theorem coeff_algebraMap_mul (U : X.Opens)
    (c : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) (y : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) (n : ℕ) :
    coeff m φ U n (algebraMap _ _ c * y) = c * coeff m φ U n y := by
  funext Z
  change (AdjoinRoot.modByMonicHom (poly_monic m φ Z.1)
      (AdjoinRoot.of _ (c Z) * y Z)).coeff n = c Z * _
  rw [← AdjoinRoot.algebraMap_eq, ← Algebra.smul_def, map_smul, Polynomial.coeff_smul,
    smul_eq_mul]
  rfl

/-- `𝓛(U) ≅ 𝒦_X(U)ᵐ` as `𝒦_X(U)`-modules, through the coefficients of `1, t, …, tᵐ⁻¹`. -/
private noncomputable def ambientEquivPi (U : X.Opens) :
    (ambient m φ).obj (op U) ≃ₗ[(rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)]
      (Fin m → (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) where
  toFun y i := coeff m φ U i y
  invFun a := reduce m φ U (∑ i : Fin m, Polynomial.monomial (i : ℕ) (a i))
  map_add' y y' := funext fun i => map_add (coeff m φ U i) y y'
  map_smul' c y := funext fun i => coeff_algebraMap_mul m φ U c y i
  left_inv y := by
    change reduce m φ U (∑ i : Fin m, Polynomial.monomial (i : ℕ) (coeff m φ U i y)) = y
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_eq_sum_range (fun n => Polynomial.monomial n (coeff m φ U n y))]
    exact reduce_sum_coeff m φ y
  right_inv a := funext fun i => by
    change coeff m φ U i (reduce m φ U (∑ i : Fin m, Polynomial.monomial (i : ℕ) (a i))) = a i
    rw [coeff_reduce_sum, dite_eq_left i.2]

end Ambient

attribute [local instance] ambientAlgebraK ambientAlgebraR isScalarTower_ambient

section CarrierLocalization

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (D : Divisor X) {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}
  (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)

include hφ in
/-- After multiplying by a nonzero regular function, every element of `𝓛(U)` lies in `𝒜(U)`. -/
private theorem exists_smul_mem_carrier {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) (z : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (s : Γ(X, U)) (hs : s ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U)) (a : (localSubalgebra m D hφ).carrier U),
      a.1 = algebraMap Γ(X, U) _ s * z := by
  classical
  have : IsFractionRing Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) :=
    isFractionRing_rationalFunctions hU hηU
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨_, hηU⟩⟩
  have : IsDomain Γ(X, U) := IsIntegral.component_integral U
  set c : Fin m → (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U) := fun i => coeff m φ U i z with hc
  choose p hp using fun i => IsLocalization.surj (nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U)) (c i)
  choose ρ hρη hρ using fun i : Fin m =>
    exists_regular_divisorialSection ((i : ℕ) • -D) hU hηU
  have hρne : ∀ i, ρ i ≠ 0 := fun i h0 => by
    have := hρη i
    rw [h0, Scheme.basicOpen_zero] at this
    exact this
  let si : Fin m → Γ(X, U) := fun i => (p i).2 * ρ i
  have hsi : ∀ i, si i ≠ 0 := fun i => mul_ne_zero (nonZeroDivisors.coe_ne_zero _) (hρne i)
  let s : Γ(X, U) := ∏ i, si i
  have hs0 : s ≠ 0 := Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ => hsi i
  have hmem : ∀ i : Fin m, algebraMap Γ(X, U) _ s * c i ∈
      ((i : ℕ) • -D).divisorialSubmodule U := by
    intro i
    have hs : s = si i * ∏ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase i, si j :=
      (Finset.mul_prod_erase _ _ (Finset.mem_univ i)).symm
    have key : algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) s * c i =
        ((∏ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase i, si j) * (p i).1) •
          (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op U) (ρ i) := by
      have h1 := hp i
      rw [Algebra.smul_def]
      change _ = algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) _ *
        algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) (ρ i)
      rw [hs, map_mul, map_mul, map_mul, ← h1]
      simp only [si, map_mul]
      ring
    rw [key]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hρ i)
  refine ⟨s, mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hs0, ⟨reduce m φ U
    (∑ i : Fin m, Polynomial.monomial (i : ℕ) (algebraMap Γ(X, U) _ s * c i)), ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · refine (mem_carrier_iff m D hφ).mpr fun n => ?_
    rw [coeff_reduce_sum]
    split_ifs with hn
    · exact hmem ⟨n, hn⟩
    · exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  · refine (ambientEquivPi m φ U).injective (funext fun i => ?_)
    change coeff m φ U i (reduce m φ U
      (∑ j : Fin m, Polynomial.monomial (j : ℕ) (algebraMap Γ(X, U) _ s * c j))) =
      coeff m φ U i (algebraMap Γ(X, U) _ s * z)
    rw [coeff_reduce_sum, dif_pos i.2]
    exact (coeff_structureMap_mul m φ s z i).symm

end CarrierLocalization

section LocalDVR

open Polynomial

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

private theorem ordGE_zero_iff_range (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (c : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)) :
    E.OrdGE 0 c ↔ ∃ r : E.localRing, E.toComponent.hom r = c := by
  constructor
  · rintro (rfl | hc)
    · exact ⟨0, map_zero _⟩
    · exact E.exists_toComponent_eq_of_one_le_valuation (by simpa using hc)
  · rintro ⟨r, rfl⟩
    by_cases hr : r = 0
    · exact Or.inl (by rw [hr, map_zero])
    · exact Or.inr (by simpa using E.one_le_valuation_toComponent hr)

private theorem ordGE_unit_mul (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    {u c : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)} {d n : ℤ}
    (hv : E.valuation u = WithZero.exp d) (hc : E.OrdGE n c) : E.OrdGE (n + d) (u * c) := by
  rcases hc with rfl | hc
  · exact Or.inl (mul_zero _)
  · refine Or.inr ?_
    calc WithZero.exp (n + d) = WithZero.exp d * WithZero.exp n := by
          rw [WithZero.exp_add, mul_comm]
      _ ≤ E.valuation u * E.valuation c := by rw [hv]; gcongr
      _ = E.valuation (u * c) := (map_mul _ _ _).symm

private theorem valuation_inv_eq (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    {u u' : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)} (huu : u * u' = 1) {d : ℤ}
    (hv : E.valuation u = WithZero.exp d) : E.valuation u' = WithZero.exp (-d) := by
  have h1 : E.valuation u * E.valuation u' = 1 := by rw [← map_mul, huu, map_one]
  rw [hv] at h1
  have h2 : WithZero.exp d * WithZero.exp (-d) = (1 : WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) := by
    rw [← WithZero.exp_add, add_neg_cancel, WithZero.exp_zero]
  exact mul_left_cancel₀ (WithZero.exp_ne_zero) (h1.trans h2.symm)

private theorem ne_zero_of_valuation_eq_exp (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    {c : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)} {d : ℤ}
    (h : E.valuation c = WithZero.exp d) : c ≠ 0 := fun h0 =>
  WithZero.exp_ne_zero (by rw [← h, h0, map_zero])

/-- An element of the local ring of a prime divisor of valuation `exp 1` is a uniformizer. -/
private theorem irreducible_of_valuation_eq_exp_one (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    {v : E.localRing} (hval : E.valuation (E.toComponent.hom v) = WithZero.exp 1) :
    Irreducible v := by
  haveI := E.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  have hv0 : v ≠ 0 := fun h0 => ne_zero_of_valuation_eq_exp E hval (by rw [h0, map_zero])
  obtain ⟨ϖ', hϖ'⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible E.localRing
  obtain ⟨k, u', hu'⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible hv0 hϖ'
  rw [hu', map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow,
    E.valuation_toComponent_of_isUnit u'.isUnit, E.valuation_toComponent_of_irreducible hϖ',
    one_mul, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul] at hval
  have hk : k = 1 := by
    have := WithZero.exp_injective hval
    simp only [nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at this
    exact_mod_cast this
  rw [hu', hk, pow_one, mul_comm]
  exact (associated_mul_unit_right ϖ' u' u'.isUnit).irreducible hϖ'

/-- **The Kummer twist at a prime divisor.** For `g` of order `d` along `E`, the function
`gᵐ φ` has order `v_E(φ) + m d`; when this is nonnegative, `gᵐ φ` lies in the local ring of `E`.
Substituting `w = g t` turns `tᵐ - φ` into `wᵐ - gᵐ φ` with integral constant term. -/
private theorem exists_kummerTwist [IsIntegral X] (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (m : ℕ)
    (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) (d : ℤ) (he : 0 ≤ E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * d) :
    ∃ (g : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X E.component)) (v : E.localRing),
      E.valuation g = WithZero.exp d ∧
      E.toComponent.hom v = g ^ m * (φ : RationalFunctions X) E.component ∧
      E.valuation (g ^ m * (φ : RationalFunctions X) E.component) =
        WithZero.exp (E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * d) := by
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := MMP.Positivity.PrimeDivisor.exists_ord_eq_one E
  have hg : E.valuation (((ϖ ^ d : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) E.component) =
      WithZero.exp d := by
    rw [E.valuation_component, E.ord_zpow, hϖ, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  have hu : E.valuation
      ((((ϖ ^ d : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) E.component) ^ m *
      (φ : RationalFunctions X) E.component) = WithZero.exp (E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * d) := by
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, hg, E.valuation_component φ, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul, ← WithZero.exp_add,
      nsmul_eq_mul, add_comm]
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := E.exists_toComponent_eq_of_one_le_valuation (by
    rw [hu, ← WithZero.exp_zero, WithZero.exp_le_exp]; exact he)
  exact ⟨_, v, hg, hv, hu⟩

variable [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}

/-- The basis `1, t, …, tᵐ⁻¹` of the fibre algebra over the function field of a component. -/
private noncomputable def kbasis (Z : irreducibleComponents X) :
    Module.Basis (Fin m) (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) (Fiber m φ Z) :=
  (AdjoinRoot.powerBasis' (poly_monic m φ Z)).basis.reindex
    (finCongr (by unfold poly; exact natDegree_X_pow_sub_C))

private theorem kbasis_repr (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (x : Fiber m φ Z) (j : Fin m) :
    (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z).repr x j =
      (AdjoinRoot.modByMonicHom (poly_monic m φ Z) x).coeff j := by
  unfold kbasis
  rw [Module.Basis.repr_reindex]
  exact AdjoinRoot.powerBasisAux'_repr_apply_to_fun _ _ _

private theorem kbasis_apply (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (j : Fin m) :
    kbasis m (φ := φ) Z j = AdjoinRoot.root (poly m φ Z) ^ (j : ℕ) := by
  unfold kbasis
  rw [Module.Basis.reindex_apply, PowerBasis.basis_eq_pow]
  rfl

variable (D : Divisor X)

/-- **Local integrality at a prime divisor.** An element `b` of `𝓛(U)` that is integral over
`𝒜(U)` has its `tⁿ`-coefficient of order `≥ n · d_E` along every prime divisor `E` meeting `U`
(here `d_E` is the coefficient of `E` in `D`), when `m` is invertible, `v_E(φ) + m d_E` is `0`
or `1`, and `tᵐ - φ` is irreducible. -/
private theorem ordGE_coeff_of_integral
    (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) {U : X.Opens} (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (hEU : (E.support ∩ U).Nonempty)
    (b : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) (p : ((ambient m φ).obj (op U))[X]) (hp : p.Monic)
    (hpc : ∀ i, p.coeff i ∈ carrier m D U) (hb : p.eval b = 0) (n : Fin m) :
    E.OrdGE (n * D.coeff E)
      (coeff m φ U n b ⟨E.component, E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU⟩) := by
  classical
  set Z := E.component
  set zi : {Z' : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z' ∈ U} :=
    ⟨Z, E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEU⟩
  let ev : (ambient m φ).obj (op U) →+* Fiber m φ Z := Pi.evalRingHom
    (fun Z' : {Z' : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z' ∈ U} =>
      Fiber m φ Z'.1) zi
  letI : Field (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z).toField
  letI : Algebra E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    E.toComponent.hom.toAlgebra
  haveI : IsFractionRing E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    isFractionRing_stalkToRationalFunctions E.genericPoint_mem_component
  haveI := E.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  have he0 : 0 ≤ E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E := by
    have := hφ E
    simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, nsmul_eq_mul, Finsupp.coe_zero,
      Pi.zero_apply] at this
    exact this
  obtain ⟨g0, v, hg0v, hv, hu0v⟩ := exists_kummerTwist E m φ (D.coeff E) he0
  have hg0 := ne_zero_of_valuation_eq_exp E hg0v
  have hu0 := ne_zero_of_valuation_eq_exp E hu0v
  set φ0 : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z) := (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z
  set e : ℤ := E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E
  have hmunit : IsUnit (m : E.localRing) := hm E.genericPoint
  let w : Fiber m φ Z := algebraMap _ (Fiber m φ Z) g0 * AdjoinRoot.root (poly m φ Z)
  have hw : w ^ m = algebraMap E.localRing (Fiber m φ Z) v := by
    have h1 : algebraMap E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) v =
        g0 ^ m * φ0 := hv
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))
      (Fiber m φ Z), h1, mul_pow, root_pow_m, map_mul, map_pow]
    rfl
  let gU : (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))ˣ := Units.mk0 g0 hg0
  let B := (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z).unitsSMul (fun i => gU ^ (i : ℕ))
  have hB : ∀ i, B i = w ^ (i : ℕ) := fun i => by
    rw [Module.Basis.unitsSMul_apply, kbasis_apply, Units.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, mul_pow,
      Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, map_pow]
    rfl
  have hwI : IsIntegral E.localRing w := by
    refine ⟨Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C v, monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m), ?_⟩
    rw [Polynomial.eval₂_sub, Polynomial.eval₂_X_pow, Polynomial.eval₂_C, hw, sub_self]
  have hBrepr : ∀ (x : Fiber m φ Z) (j : Fin m), B.repr x j =
      (g0 ^ (j : ℕ))⁻¹ * (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z).repr x j := by
    intro x j
    have := congrArg (fun f => f x) (Module.Basis.coord_unitsSMul (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z)
      (fun i => gU ^ (i : ℕ)) j)
    simp only [Module.Basis.coord_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply] at this
    refine this.trans ?_
    rw [Units.smul_def, smul_eq_mul]
    simp [gU]
  have hkrepr : ∀ (a : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) (j : Fin m),
      (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z).repr (ev a) j = coeff m φ U j a zi := fun a j => by
    rw [kbasis_repr]; rfl
  have hord : ∀ a ∈ carrier m D U, ∀ j : Fin m,
      E.OrdGE (j * D.coeff E) (coeff m φ U j a zi) := fun a ha j => by
    have hmem := (mem_carrier_iff m D hφ).mp ha j
    have := hmem E hEU
    have e1 : -(((j : ℕ) • -D).coeff E) = (j : ℤ) * D.coeff E := by
      simp [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_smul]
    rw [e1] at this
    exact this
  have hg0pow : ∀ j : ℕ, E.valuation (g0 ^ j) = WithZero.exp ((j : ℤ) * D.coeff E) := fun j => by
    rw [map_pow, hg0v, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul]
    simp
  have hg0inv : ∀ j : ℕ, E.valuation ((g0 ^ j)⁻¹) = WithZero.exp (-((j : ℤ) * D.coeff E)) :=
    fun j => valuation_inv_eq E (mul_inv_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero j hg0)) (hg0pow j)
  have hcoord : ∀ a ∈ carrier m D U, ∀ j : Fin m,
      ∃ r : E.localRing, B.repr (ev a) j = algebraMap E.localRing _ r := fun a ha j => by
    have h1 := ordGE_unit_mul E (hg0inv j) (hord a ha j)
    rw [add_neg_cancel, ordGE_zero_iff_range] at h1
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := h1
    exact ⟨r, by rw [hBrepr, hkrepr]; exact hr.symm⟩
  have hI : ∀ a ∈ carrier m D U, IsIntegral E.localRing (ev a) := fun a ha => by
    choose r hr using hcoord a ha
    rw [← B.sum_repr (ev a)]
    refine IsIntegral.sum _ fun j _ => ?_
    rw [hr j, hB, algebraMap_smul _, Algebra.smul_def]
    exact isIntegral_algebraMap.mul (hwI.pow _)
  have hbI : IsIntegral E.localRing (ev b) := by
    set q : (Fiber m φ Z)[X] := p.map ev with hq
    have hqm : q.Monic := hp.map ev
    have hqe : q.eval (ev b) = 0 := by
      rw [hq, Polynomial.eval_map]
      have := Polynomial.hom_eval₂ p (RingHom.id _) ev b
      rw [RingHom.comp_id] at this
      rw [← this]
      change ev (p.eval b) = 0
      rw [hb, map_zero]
    by_cases hdeg : q.natDegree = 0
    · have h1 : q = 1 := (Polynomial.Monic.natDegree_eq_zero hqm).mp hdeg
      rw [h1, Polynomial.eval_one] at hqe
      have : ev b = 0 := (subsingleton_of_zero_eq_one hqe.symm).elim _ _
      rw [this]
      exact isIntegral_zero
    · refine IsIntegral.of_aeval_monic_of_isIntegral_coeff hqm hdeg (by rw [hqe]; exact
        isIntegral_zero) fun i => ?_
      rw [hq, Polynomial.coeff_map]
      exact hI _ (hpc i)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ : ∃ r : E.localRing, B.repr (ev b) n = algebraMap E.localRing _ r := by
    rcases (show e = 0 ∨ e = 1 by have := h01 E; omega) with he' | he'
    · obtain ⟨v', hv'⟩ := E.exists_toComponent_eq_of_one_le_valuation (f := (g0 ^ m * φ0)⁻¹)
        (by rw [map_inv₀, hu0v, he']; simp)
      have hvunit : IsUnit v := by
        refine IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one v' (a := v) (IsFractionRing.injective E.localRing
          (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) ?_)
        change E.toComponent.hom (v * v') = E.toComponent.hom 1
        rw [map_mul, hv, hv', map_one]
        exact mul_inv_cancel₀ hu0
      exact KummerBasis.coords_mem m hmunit v hvunit w hw B hB (ev b) hbI n
    · have hvirr : Irreducible v :=
        irreducible_of_valuation_eq_exp_one E (by rw [hv, hu0v, he'])
      letI : Fact (Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) := ⟨hirr Z⟩
      exact KummerBasis.coords_mem_of_irreducible m v hvirr w hw B hB (ev b) hbI n
  have h3 : (kbasis m (φ := φ) Z).repr (ev b) n = g0 ^ (n : ℕ) * algebraMap E.localRing _ r := by
    rw [← hr, hBrepr, ← mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero _ hg0), one_mul]
  rw [hkrepr] at h3
  have h4 : E.OrdGE 0 (algebraMap E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) r) :=
    (ordGE_zero_iff_range E _).mpr ⟨r, rfl⟩
  have h5 := ordGE_unit_mul E (hg0pow n) h4
  rw [zero_add, ← h3] at h5
  exact h5

end LocalDVR

section Branch

open Polynomial

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (D : Divisor X) {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}

/-- **`tᵐ - φ` is irreducible over `K(X)` when it is branched to order one along a prime
divisor.** If `v_E(φ) + m d_E = 1`, then with `g` of order `d_E` along `E` the polynomial
`Tᵐ - gᵐ φ` is Eisenstein over the discrete valuation ring of `E`, and `t = g⁻¹ T`. -/
private theorem irreducible_poly (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (hE : E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E = 1) (Z : irreducibleComponents X) :
    Irreducible (poly m φ Z) := by
  classical
  obtain rfl : Z = E.component := (eq_theComponent Z).trans (eq_theComponent _).symm
  set Z := E.component
  letI : Field (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z).toField
  letI : Algebra E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    E.toComponent.hom.toAlgebra
  haveI : IsFractionRing E.localRing (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    isFractionRing_stalkToRationalFunctions E.genericPoint_mem_component
  haveI := E.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  obtain ⟨g0, v, hg0v, hv, hu0v⟩ := exists_kummerTwist E m φ (D.coeff E) (hE ▸ zero_le_one)
  have hg0 := ne_zero_of_valuation_eq_exp E hg0v
  set φ0 : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z) := (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z
  have hvirr : Irreducible v := irreducible_of_valuation_eq_exp_one E (by rw [hv, hu0v, hE])
  have hv0 := hvirr.ne_zero
  -- `Tᵐ - v` is irreducible over `E.localRing`, hence over `K(X)`
  have hq : Irreducible (Polynomial.X ^ m - C v : E.localRing[X]) := by
    refine (KummerBasis.isEisensteinAt_X_pow_sub_C hvirr m).irreducible ?_
      (monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m)).isPrimitive ?_
    · exact (Ideal.span_singleton_prime hv0).mpr hvirr.prime
    · rw [natDegree_X_pow_sub_C]; exact NeZero.pos m
  have hqK : Irreducible (Polynomial.X ^ m - C (g0 ^ m * φ0) :
      (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))[X]) := by
    have := ((monic_X_pow_sub_C v (NeZero.ne m)).irreducible_iff_irreducible_map_fraction_map
      (K := X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))).mp hq
    rwa [Polynomial.map_sub, Polynomial.map_pow, map_X, map_C, show algebraMap E.localRing _ v =
      g0 ^ m * φ0 from hv] at this
  -- rescale `T = g₀ t`
  letI : Invertible g0 := invertibleOfNonzero hg0
  have himg : algEquivCMulXAddC g0 0 (Polynomial.X ^ m - C (g0 ^ m * φ0)) =
      C (g0 ^ m) * poly m φ Z := by
    rw [algEquivCMulXAddC_apply, map_sub, map_pow, aeval_X, aeval_C, map_zero, add_zero, mul_pow,
      ← C_pow, poly, mul_sub, ← C_mul, Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
  have h1 := (MulEquiv.irreducible_iff (algEquivCMulXAddC g0 0).toMulEquiv).mpr hqK
  change Irreducible (algEquivCMulXAddC g0 0 _) at h1
  rw [himg] at h1
  exact (associated_unit_mul_left (poly m φ Z) (C (g0 ^ m))
    ((isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr (pow_ne_zero m hg0)).map C)).irreducible h1

end Branch

section Normality

open Polynomial

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (D : Divisor X) {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}

/-- `𝒜(U)` is a subalgebra of `𝓛(U)`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def carrierAlgebra (U : X.Opens) :
    Algebra ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) :=
  (carrier (φ := φ) m D U).subtype.toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] carrierAlgebra

/-- `𝒜(U)` is integrally closed in `𝓛(U)`. -/
private theorem mem_carrier_of_integral (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) {U : X.Opens} (b : (ambient m φ).obj (op U))
    (p : ((ambient m φ).obj (op U))[X]) (hp : p.Monic) (hpc : ∀ i, p.coeff i ∈ carrier m D U)
    (hb : p.eval b = 0) : b ∈ carrier m D U := by
  rw [mem_carrier_iff m D hφ]
  intro n
  by_cases hn : n < m
  · intro E hEU
    have := ordGE_coeff_of_integral m D hm hφ h01 hirr E hEU b p hp hpc hb ⟨n, hn⟩
    have e1 : -(((n : ℕ) • -D).coeff E) = (((⟨n, hn⟩ : Fin m) : ℕ) : ℤ) * D.coeff E := by
      simp [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_smul]
    rw [e1]
    exact this
  · rw [coeff_eq_zero_of_le m φ b (not_lt.mp hn)]
    exact zero_mem _

private theorem isIntegrallyClosedIn_carrier (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) (U : X.Opens) :
    IsIntegrallyClosedIn ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
  refine (isIntegrallyClosedIn_iff (R := carrier (φ := φ) m D U) (A := (ambient m φ).obj (op
      U))).mpr
    ⟨Subtype.val_injective, fun {b} hb => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpe⟩ := hb
  have hb' : b ∈ carrier m D U := by
    refine mem_carrier_of_integral m D hm hφ h01 hirr b
        (p.map (algebraMap (carrier (φ := φ) m D U) _))
        (hp.map _)
      (fun i => ?_) (by rw [Polynomial.eval_map]; exact hpe)
    rw [Polynomial.coeff_map]
    exact (p.coeff i).2
  exact ⟨⟨b, hb'⟩, rfl⟩

/-- `𝓛(U)` is an Artinian ring: a finite product of finite algebras over fields. -/
private theorem isArtinianRing_ambient (U : X.Opens) :
    IsArtinianRing ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
  have : ∀ Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U},
      IsArtinianRing (Fiber m φ Z.1) := fun Z => by
    letI : Field (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z.1)) :=
      (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z.1).toField
    have : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z.1)) (Fiber m φ Z.1) :=
      (poly_monic m φ Z.1).finite_adjoinRoot
    exact IsArtinianRing.of_finite (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z.1)) _
  have : Finite {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U} := by
    have : AlgebraicGeometry.IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    have : Finite (irreducibleComponents X) :=
      (NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents (α := X)).to_subtype
    infer_instance
  exact (inferInstance : IsArtinianRing (∀ Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X //
    componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U}, Fiber m φ Z.1))

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] in
/-- The fibre `K(X)[t]/(tᵐ - φ)` of an irreducible `tᵐ - φ` is a field. -/
private theorem isField_fiber (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hirr : Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) :
    IsField (Fiber m φ Z) := by
  letI : Field (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :=
    (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z).toField
  haveI : Fact (Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) := ⟨hirr⟩
  exact Field.toIsField (AdjoinRoot (poly m φ Z))

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] in
/-- `𝓛(U)` is reduced: each factor is a field. -/
private theorem isReduced_ambient (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z))
    (U : X.Opens) : IsReduced ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
  have : ∀ Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U},
      IsReduced (Fiber m φ Z.1) := fun Z => by
    letI := (isField_fiber m Z.1 (hirr Z.1)).toField
    infer_instance
  exact (inferInstance : IsReduced (∀ Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X //
    componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U}, Fiber m φ Z.1))

/-- `𝓛(U)` is the total ring of fractions of `𝒜(U)`. -/
private theorem isLocalization_carrier (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    IsLocalization (nonZeroDivisors ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
  have : IsArtinianRing ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := isArtinianRing_ambient m U
  have hFR : IsFractionRing Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) :=
    isFractionRing_rationalFunctions hU hηU
  have hρ : ∀ ρ ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U), IsUnit (algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U))
      ρ) := by
    intro ρ hρ
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U))
      ((ambient m φ).obj (op U))]
    exact (IsLocalization.map_units ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) ⟨ρ, hρ⟩).map _
  refine ⟨fun s => ?_, fun z => ?_, fun {x y} hxy => ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
  · have hnz : ((s : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)) : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ∈
        nonZeroDivisors ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
      rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left]
      intro z hz
      obtain ⟨ρ, hρn, a, ha⟩ : ∃ (ρ : Γ(X, U)) (_ : ρ ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U))
        (a : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)), a.1 = algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ *
            z :=
      exists_smul_mem_carrier m D hφ hU hηU z
      have h1 : (s : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)) * a = 0 := by
        apply Subtype.ext
        change ((s : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)) : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) * a.1 = 0
        rw [ha, mul_left_comm, hz, mul_zero]
      have h2 : a = 0 := (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mp s.2) a h1
      have h3 : algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ * z = 0 := by
        rw [← ha, h2]; rfl
      exact (hρ ρ hρn).mul_right_eq_zero.mp h3
    exact IsArtinianRing.isUnit_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors hnz
  · obtain ⟨ρ, hρn, a, ha⟩ : ∃ (ρ : Γ(X, U)) (_ : ρ ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U))
        (a : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)), a.1 = algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ *
            z :=
      exists_smul_mem_carrier m D hφ hU hηU z
    let ρS : ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := (localSubalgebra m D hφ).algebraMap U ρ
    have hρS : ρS ∈ nonZeroDivisors ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := by
      rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left]
      intro y hy
      have h3 : algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ * y.1 = 0 := by
        have := congrArg Subtype.val hy
        change (ρS : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) * y.1 = 0 at this
        rwa [show (ρS : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) = algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ
          from LocalSubalgebra.coe_algebraMap (localSubalgebra m D hφ) U ρ] at this
      exact Subtype.ext ((hρ ρ hρn).mul_right_eq_zero.mp h3)
    refine ⟨(a, ⟨_, hρS⟩), ?_⟩
    change z * (ρS : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) = a.1
    rw [show (ρS : (ambient m φ).obj (op U)) = algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ρ
      from LocalSubalgebra.coe_algebraMap (localSubalgebra m D hφ) U ρ, ha, mul_comm]
  · have := Subtype.ext hxy
    rw [this]

/-- `𝒜(U)` is a finite `Γ(X, U)`-module, for `U` affine. -/
private theorem finite_algebraMap_carrier {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D) :
    ((localSubalgebra m D hφ).algebraMap U).Finite := by
  letI := (localSubalgebra m D hφ).moduleSections U
  have : ∀ i : Fin m, Module.Finite Γ(X, U) Γ((((i : ℕ) • -D)).divisorialSheaf, U) :=
    fun i => finite_divisorialSubmodule _ hU
  exact Module.Finite.equiv (coeffLinearEquiv m D hφ U).symm

/-- **`𝒜(U)` is a normal ring.** -/
private theorem isNormalRing_carrier (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) : IsNormalRing ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := by
  haveI := isLocalization_carrier m D hφ hU hηU
  haveI : IsIntegrallyClosed ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) :=
    (isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosedIn ((ambient m φ).obj (op U))).mpr
      (isIntegrallyClosedIn_carrier m D hm hφ h01 hirr U)
  haveI : IsReduced ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := isReduced_ambient m hirr U
  haveI : IsReduced ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) :=
    isReduced_of_injective (carrier (φ := φ) m D U).subtype Subtype.val_injective
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨_, hηU⟩⟩
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  have hfin : (minimalPrimes ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U)).Finite := by
    letI : Algebra Γ(X, U) ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) :=
      ((localSubalgebra m D hφ).algebraMap U).toAlgebra
    haveI : Module.Finite Γ(X, U) ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := finite_algebraMap_carrier m D hU hφ
    haveI : IsNoetherian Γ(X, U) ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) :=
      isNoetherian_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite Γ(X, U) _
    haveI : IsNoetherianRing ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) :=
      isNoetherian_of_tower Γ(X, U) inferInstance
    exact minimalPrimes.finite_of_isNoetherianRing _
  have hic : IsIntegrallyClosed ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := inferInstance
  exact ((isIntegrallyClosed_tfae_of_finite_minimalPrimes hfin).out 2 1).mp hic

end Normality

section Chart

open CategoryTheory.Limits

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (D : Divisor X) {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}
  (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)

/-- `𝒜(U) ≃ Γ(X', p⁻¹U)` over an affine open `U`. -/
private noncomputable def psiEquiv {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (localSubalgebra m D hφ).carrier U ≃+*
      Γ(cover m D hφ, toBase m D hφ ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective
    ((Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap (situation m D hφ)).right.app (op U)).hom (by
      have := Stacks.RelativeSpec.isIso_universalAlgebraMap_app (situation m D hφ) ⟨U, hU⟩
      exact ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _)

end Chart

section CoverScheme

/-- An affine open with domain sections is an irreducible subset. -/
private theorem isIrreducible_of_isAffineOpen {Y : Scheme.{u}} {V : Y.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    [IsDomain Γ(Y, V)] : IsIrreducible (V : Set Y) := by
  haveI : IsAffine V.toScheme := hV
  let e : Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) ≃+* Γ(Y, V) := V.topIso.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  haveI : IsDomain Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) := Function.Injective.isDomain e.toRingHom e.injective
  have hne : (V : Set Y).Nonempty := by
    rw [Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty]
    intro h0
    have hsub : Subsingleton Γ(Y, V) := by
      rw [show V = ⊥ from Opens.ext h0]
      infer_instance
    exact @not_subsingleton _ IsDomain.toNontrivial hsub
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hne
  haveI : Nonempty V.toScheme := ⟨⟨x, hx⟩⟩
  haveI := isIntegral_of_isAffine_of_isDomain V.toScheme
  have := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ V.toScheme).image V.ι V.ι.continuous.continuousOn
  rwa [Set.image_univ, Scheme.Opens.range_ι] at this

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (D : Divisor X) {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}
  (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • D)

private theorem isAffineHom_toBase : IsAffineHom (toBase m D hφ) := by
  haveI := (situation m D hφ).isQuasicoherent
  exact Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.isAffineHom_relativeSpecToBase (situation m D hφ).algebra

/-- Finiteness: `𝒜` is a finite direct sum of coherent divisorial sheaves. -/
private theorem isFinite_toBase : IsFinite (toBase m D hφ) := by
  haveI := (situation m D hφ).isQuasicoherent
  haveI := isAffineHom_toBase m D hφ
  refine ⟨fun U hU => ?_⟩
  have hI : (((Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap (situation m D hφ)).right.app
      (op U)).hom).Finite := by
    have := Stacks.RelativeSpec.isIso_universalAlgebraMap_app (situation m D hφ) ⟨U, hU⟩
    exact RingHom.Finite.of_surjective _
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
        ((Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap (situation m D hφ)).right.app (op U))).2
  rw [Stacks.RelativeSpec.toBase_app]
  exact hI.comp (finite_algebraMap_carrier m D hU hφ)

/-- The generic point lies in every nonempty open of `X`. -/
private theorem genericPoint_mem_of_ne_bot {U : X.Opens} (hU : U ≠ ⊥) : genericPoint X ∈ U := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (Opens.ne_bot_iff_nonempty U).mp hU
  exact ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes (Set.mem_univ y)).mem_open U.isOpen hy

/-- **Normality of the cover.** -/
private theorem isNormal_cover (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) : IsNormal (cover m D hφ) := by
  haveI := (situation m D hφ).isQuasicoherent
  haveI := isAffineHom_toBase m D hφ
  refine ((isNormal_tfae (cover m D hφ)).out 3 1).mp ?_
  refine ⟨X.affineOpens, fun U => ⟨toBase m D hφ ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, U.2.preimage _⟩, ?_, fun U => ?_⟩
  · rw [IsOpenCover, eq_top_iff]
    intro x _
    have hx : (toBase m D hφ) x ∈ ⨆ U : X.affineOpens, (U : X.Opens) := by
      rw [iSup_affineOpens_eq_top X]; trivial
    obtain ⟨U, hU⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp hx
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨U, hU⟩
  · by_cases hη : genericPoint X ∈ U.1
    · exact IsNormalRing.congr (psiEquiv m D hφ U.2)
        (isNormalRing_carrier m D hm hφ h01 hirr U.2 hη)
    · have hU0 : U.1 = ⊥ := by
        by_contra hne
        exact hη (genericPoint_mem_of_ne_bot hne)
      have hV : (toBase m D hφ) ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 = ⊥ := by rw [hU0]; exact Scheme.Hom.preimage_bot _
      have : Subsingleton Γ(cover m D hφ, (toBase m D hφ) ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := by
        rw [hV]
        infer_instance
      intro q hq
      exact absurd (Subsingleton.elim q ⊤) hq.ne_top

omit [CompactSpace X] in
/-- `𝓛(U)` is a field, hence a domain, when `tᵐ - φ` is irreducible and `η ∈ U`. -/
private theorem isDomain_ambient (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) {U : X.Opens}
    (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) : IsDomain ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) := by
  letI := uniqueComponent hηU
  let e : ((ambient m φ).obj (op U)) ≃+* Fiber m φ
      (default : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U}).1 :=
    RingEquiv.piUnique _
  haveI : IsDomain (Fiber m φ
      (default : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U}).1) :=
    (isField_fiber m _ (hirr _)).isDomain
  exact Function.Injective.isDomain e.toRingHom e.injective

private theorem isDomain_sections (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hηU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    IsDomain Γ(cover m D hφ, toBase m D hφ ⁻¹ᵁ U) := by
  haveI := isDomain_ambient m hirr hηU
  haveI : IsDomain ↥(carrier (φ := φ) m D U) := inferInstance
  exact Function.Injective.isDomain (psiEquiv m D hφ hU).symm.toRingHom
    (psiEquiv m D hφ hU).symm.injective

/-- **The cover is integral** when `tᵐ - φ` is irreducible: it is covered by the irreducible
affine opens `p⁻¹U`, any two of which meet. -/
private theorem isIntegral_cover (hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * D.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (hirr : ∀ Z, Irreducible (poly m φ Z)) : IsIntegral (cover m D hφ) := by
  haveI := (situation m D hφ).isQuasicoherent
  haveI := isAffineHom_toBase m D hφ
  haveI := isNormal_cover m D hφ hm h01 hirr
  set p := toBase m D hφ
  have hirrU : ∀ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → genericPoint X ∈ U →
      IsIrreducible ((p ⁻¹ᵁ U : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ)) := fun U hU hηU => by
    haveI := isDomain_sections m D hφ hirr hU hηU
    exact isIrreducible_of_isAffineOpen (hU.preimage p)
  -- every point lies in some `p⁻¹U` with `U` affine
  have hcov : ∀ z : cover m D hφ, ∃ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U ∧ genericPoint X ∈ U ∧
      z ∈ p ⁻¹ᵁ U := fun z => by
    obtain ⟨U, hU, hzU, -⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
      (show p z ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
    refine ⟨U, hU, genericPoint_mem_of_ne_bot ?_, hzU⟩
    rintro rfl
    exact hzU
  have key : ∀ (A : (cover m D hφ).Opens) (U U' : X.Opens), IsAffineOpen U → IsAffineOpen U' →
      genericPoint X ∈ U → genericPoint X ∈ U' → U' ≤ U →
      ((A : Set (cover m D hφ)) ∩
        ((p ⁻¹ᵁ U : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ))).Nonempty →
      ((A : Set (cover m D hφ)) ∩
        ((p ⁻¹ᵁ U' : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ))).Nonempty := by
    intro A U U' hU hU' hηU hηU' hle hA
    have h2 : (((p ⁻¹ᵁ U : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ)) ∩
        ((p ⁻¹ᵁ U' : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ))).Nonempty := by
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (hirrU U' hU' hηU').nonempty
      exact ⟨c, (p.preimage_mono hle) hc, hc⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc1, hc2, hc3⟩ := (hirrU U hU hηU).2 (A : Set (cover m D hφ))
      ((p ⁻¹ᵁ U' : (cover m D hφ).Opens) : Set (cover m D hφ)) A.isOpen (Opens.isOpen _)
      (by rwa [Set.inter_comm]) h2
    exact ⟨c, hc2, hc3⟩
  haveI : IrreducibleSpace (cover m D hφ) := by
    refine (irreducibleSpace_def _).mpr ⟨?_, fun A B hA hB hAa hBb => ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨U, hU, hηU, -⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
        (show genericPoint X ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (hirrU U hU hηU).nonempty
      exact ⟨c, trivial⟩
    · obtain ⟨a, -, ha⟩ := hAa
      obtain ⟨b, -, hb⟩ := hBb
      obtain ⟨Ua, hUa, hηa, haU⟩ := hcov a
      obtain ⟨Ub, hUb, hηb, hbU⟩ := hcov b
      obtain ⟨U', hU', hηU', hle⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
        (show genericPoint X ∈ Ua ⊓ Ub from ⟨hηa, hηb⟩)
      have hA' := key ⟨A, hA⟩ Ua U' hUa hU' hηa hηU' (hle.trans inf_le_left) ⟨a, ha, haU⟩
      have hB' := key ⟨B, hB⟩ Ub U' hUb hU' hηb hηU' (hle.trans inf_le_right) ⟨b, hb, hbU⟩
      obtain ⟨c, hc1, hcA, hcB⟩ := (hirrU U' hU' hηU').2 A B hA hB
        (by rw [Set.inter_comm]; exact hA') (by rw [Set.inter_comm]; exact hB')
      exact ⟨c, trivial, hcA, hcB⟩
  exact isIntegral_of_irreducibleSpace_of_isReduced _

end CoverScheme

section Trivialization

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  {D : Divisor X} {W : X.Opens} {ψ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}

/-- The restriction to `W` of a global unit of `K(X)`. -/
private noncomputable def unitOn (W : X.Opens) (ψ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) :
    ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op W)) :=
  fun Z => (ψ : RationalFunctions X) Z.1

/-- The local frame `ψ⁻¹` of `𝒪_X(D)` on an open where `ψ` is a local equation of `D`. -/
private noncomputable def frame (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) : Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) :=
  (⟨unitOn W ψ⁻¹, fun E hE => Or.inr (by
    change WithZero.exp _ ≤ E.valuation
      (((ψ⁻¹ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) E.component)
    rw [E.valuation_component, PrimeDivisor.ord_inv, hψ E hE])⟩ : D.divisorialSubmodule W)

omit [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] in
private theorem secVal_frame (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) :
    Divisor.secVal D W (frame hψ) = unitOn W ψ⁻¹ := rfl

omit [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] in
private theorem secVal_smul (r : Γ(X, W)) (a : Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W)) :
    Divisor.secVal D W (r • a) = (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op W) r *
      Divisor.secVal D W a := by
  funext Z
  exact rationalFunctions_smul_apply r _ Z

/-- Multiplication of a regular function by the frame `ψ⁻¹`, `𝒪_W ⟶ 𝒪_X(D)|_W`. -/
private noncomputable def frameMap (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) :
    Γ(X, W) →ₗ[Γ(X, W)] Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) :=
  LinearMap.toSpanSingleton Γ(X, W) Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) (frame hψ)

omit [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] in
private theorem unitOn_mul_unitOn_inv (W : X.Opens) (ψ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) :
    unitOn W ψ * unitOn W ψ⁻¹ = 1 := by
  funext Z
  change (ψ : RationalFunctions X) Z.1 * ((ψ⁻¹ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) Z.1
    = 1
  rw [← Pi.mul_apply, ← Units.val_mul, mul_inv_cancel, Units.val_one, Pi.one_apply]

omit [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] in
private theorem frameMap_bijective (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) :
    Function.Bijective (frameMap hψ) := by
  refine ⟨fun r r' h => ?_, fun a => ?_⟩
  · apply toRationalFunctionsPresheaf_app_injective W
    have h1 := congrArg (fun b : Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) => Divisor.secVal D W b * unitOn W ψ) h
    simp only [frameMap, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply] at h1
    rw [secVal_smul, secVal_smul, secVal_frame, mul_assoc, mul_assoc, mul_comm (unitOn W ψ⁻¹),
      unitOn_mul_unitOn_inv, mul_one, mul_one] at h1
    exact h1
  · let a' : D.divisorialSubmodule W := a
    have hb : (0 : Divisor X).IsDivisorialSection W (unitOn W ψ * Divisor.secVal D W a) := by
      intro E hE
      have hψE : E.OrdGE (E.ord ψ) ((ψ : RationalFunctions X) E.component) :=
        Or.inr (E.valuation_component ψ).ge
      refine (hψE.mul (a'.2 E hE)).mono (le_of_eq ?_)
      rw [hψ E hE]
      simp
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Divisor.IsDivisorialSection.exists_eq hb
    refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
    apply Subtype.ext
    change Divisor.secVal D W (r • frame hψ) = Divisor.secVal D W a
    rw [secVal_smul, secVal_frame, hr, mul_comm, ← mul_assoc, mul_comm _ (unitOn W ψ),
      unitOn_mul_unitOn_inv, one_mul]

/-- The trivialization `𝒪_X(D)|_W ≅ 𝒪_W` given by a local equation `ψ` of `D` on `W`. -/
private noncomputable def trivialization (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) :
    Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, W)] Γ(X, W) :=
  (LinearEquiv.ofBijective (frameMap hψ) (frameMap_bijective hψ)).symm

omit [IsIntegral X] [CompactSpace X] in
/-- The function representing a section `a` of `𝒪_X(D)` on `W` is `ψ a`. -/
private theorem toRationalFunctions_trivialization (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ)
    (a : Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W)) :
    (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op W) (trivialization hψ a) =
      unitOn W ψ * Divisor.secVal D W a := by
  have h := (LinearEquiv.ofBijective (frameMap hψ) (frameMap_bijective hψ)).apply_symm_apply a
  set r := trivialization hψ a
  have h1 : frameMap hψ r = a := h
  have h2 := congrArg (fun b : Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, W) => unitOn W ψ * Divisor.secVal D W b) h1
  simp only [frameMap, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply] at h2
  rw [← h2, secVal_smul, secVal_frame, mul_comm, mul_assoc, mul_comm (unitOn W ψ⁻¹),
    unitOn_mul_unitOn_inv, mul_one]

end Trivialization

/-- In a domain, if `a = u ϖ^m` with `ϖ` irreducible and `(a)` is a radical ideal, then
`m ≤ 1`: otherwise `ϖ^{m-1} ∉ (a)` while `(ϖ^{m-1})² ∈ (a)`. -/
private theorem le_one_of_radical_span_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    {ϖ a : R} (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ) (u : Rˣ) (m : ℕ) (ha : a = u * ϖ ^ m)
    (hrad : (Ideal.span {a}).radical = Ideal.span {a}) : m ≤ 1 := by
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ : ∃ j, m = j + 2 := ⟨m - 2, by omega⟩
  have hmem : ϖ ^ (j + 1) ∈ (Ideal.span {a}).radical := by
    refine ⟨2, Ideal.mem_span_singleton.2 ⟨(u⁻¹ : Rˣ) * ϖ ^ j, ?_⟩⟩
    rw [ha]
    calc (ϖ ^ (j + 1)) ^ 2 = (u * (u⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R) * ϖ ^ (j + 2) * ϖ ^ j := by
          rw [Units.mul_inv, one_mul]; ring
      _ = _ := by ring
  rw [hrad, Ideal.mem_span_singleton, ha] at hmem
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hmem
  have hϖ0 : ϖ ≠ 0 := hϖ.ne_zero
  have h1 : ϖ ^ (j + 1) * (1 - u * ϖ * c) = 0 := by
    rw [mul_sub, mul_one, sub_eq_zero]
    calc ϖ ^ (j + 1) = u * ϖ ^ (j + 2) * c := hc
      _ = _ := by ring
  rcases mul_eq_zero.1 h1 with h | h
  · exact hϖ0 (pow_eq_zero_iff (Nat.succ_ne_zero j) |>.1 h)
  · apply hϖ.not_isUnit
    rw [sub_eq_zero] at h
    exact IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one (u * c) (by rw [h]; ring)

/-- A principal radical ideal of the sections over an affine open stays radical in each stalk,
the stalk being a localization. -/
private theorem radical_span_germ_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (g : Γ(X, U)) (h : (Ideal.span {g}).radical = Ideal.span {g}) (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U) :
    (Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U y hy).hom g}).radical =
      Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U y hy).hom g} := by
  letI := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨y, hy⟩
  have := hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨y, hy⟩
  have hmap := IsLocalization.map_radical (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl
    (X.presheaf.stalk y) (Ideal.span {g})
  rw [h, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton] at hmap
  exact hmap.symm

section ZeroScheme

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
  {D : Divisor X}

omit [CompactSpace X] in
/-- The function representing `σ|_W` in the trivialization by a local equation `ψ` of `D` has
component `ψ_Z σ_Z` at the irreducible component `Z`. -/
private theorem germ_trivialization_restrict {W : X.Opens} {ψ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}
    (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) (σ : D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤)
    (Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ W}) :
    X.presheaf.germ W _ Z.2 (trivialization hψ
        (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)) =
      (ψ : RationalFunctions X) Z.1 * σ.1 ⟨Z.1, trivial⟩ :=
  congrFun (toRationalFunctions_trivialization hψ
    (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)) Z

/-- **A section with reduced zero scheme has a reduced divisor of zeros.** If `D` is Cartier and
the zero scheme of a nonzero section `σ` of `𝒪_X(D)` is reduced, every coefficient of
`(σ)₀ = div σ + D` is at most `1`: at the generic point of a prime divisor `E` the ideal of the
zero scheme is `(π^a)` with `a` the coefficient, and it is radical only for `a ≤ 1`. -/
private theorem coeff_zeroDivisor_le_one (hD : D.IsCartier)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property D.divisorialSheaf]
    (σ : D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤) (hσ : σ ≠ 0)
    (hred : IsReduced (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X D.divisorialSheaf σ).subscheme)
    (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).coeff E ≤ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, ψ, hψ⟩ := hD E.genericPoint
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWU⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens) hxU
  have hψW := hψ.mono hWU
  set r := trivialization hψW (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)
    with hr
  have hideal :
      (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X D.divisorialSheaf σ).ideal ⟨W, hW⟩ = Ideal.span {r} :=
    zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X D.divisorialSheaf σ ⟨W, hW⟩ (trivialization hψW) r rfl
  have hrad := Stacks.Models.radical_eq_self_of_isReduced_subscheme
    (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X D.divisorialSheaf σ)
  have hWrad : (Ideal.span {r}).radical = Ideal.span {r} := by
    have := congrArg (fun J : X.IdealSheafData => J.ideal ⟨W, hW⟩) hrad
    simp only [Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal] at this
    rwa [hideal] at this
  have hst := radical_span_germ_eq hW r hWrad E.genericPoint hxW
  haveI := E.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible E.localRing
  set a : E.localRing := (X.presheaf.germ W E.genericPoint hxW).hom r with ha
  have hEW : (E.support ∩ W).Nonempty := ⟨E.genericPoint, by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
    exact subset_closure rfl, hxW⟩
  have hZW := E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hEW
  set φσ := (Divisor.isUnit_sectionToRationalFunctions hσ).unit
  have hcoeff : (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).coeff E = E.ord φσ + E.ord ψ := by
    rw [Divisor.zeroDivisor_eq, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_add, coeff_principalDivisor, hψW E hEW]
  have hval : E.valuation (E.toComponent.hom a) =
      WithZero.exp ((D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).coeff E) := by
    have h1 : E.toComponent.hom a = X.presheaf.germ W _ hZW r :=
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply X.presheaf hxW E.specializes_genericPoint r
    rw [h1, germ_trivialization_restrict hψW σ ⟨E.component, hZW⟩]
    have h2 : σ.1 ⟨E.component, trivial⟩ = (φσ : RationalFunctions X) E.component := by
      rw [IsUnit.unit_spec]; rfl
    rw [h2, map_mul, E.valuation_component ψ, E.valuation_component φσ, ← WithZero.exp_add,
      hcoeff, add_comm]
  have ha0 : a ≠ 0 := fun h0 => by
    rw [h0, map_zero, map_zero] at hval
    exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero hval.symm
  obtain ⟨n, u, hau⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible ha0 hϖ
  have hn := le_one_of_radical_span_eq hϖ u n hau hst
  rw [hau, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow, E.valuation_toComponent_of_isUnit u.isUnit,
    E.valuation_toComponent_of_irreducible hϖ, one_mul, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul] at hval
  have := WithZero.exp_injective hval
  rw [← this]
  simp only [nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  exact_mod_cast hn

/-- On an open meeting no component of the support of `(σ)₀`, the trivializing function of `σ`
is a unit. -/
private theorem isUnit_trivialization_restrict {W : X.Opens} {ψ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ}
    (hψ : D.IsLocalEquation W ψ) (σ : D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤) (hσ : σ ≠ 0)
    (hW : ∀ y ∈ W, y ∉ (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).supp) :
    IsUnit (trivialization hψ
      (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)) := by
  set φσ := (Divisor.isUnit_sectionToRationalFunctions hσ).unit
  set r := trivialization hψ (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)
  have hr : ∀ Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ W},
      (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op W) r Z = ((ψ * φσ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) :
        RationalFunctions X) Z.1 := fun Z => by
    rw [toRationalFunctionsPresheaf_app_apply, germ_trivialization_restrict hψ σ Z]
    have h2 : σ.1 ⟨Z.1, trivial⟩ = (φσ : RationalFunctions X) Z.1 := by
      rw [IsUnit.unit_spec]; rfl
    rw [h2, Units.val_mul, Pi.mul_apply]
  have hinv : (0 : Divisor X).IsDivisorialSection W (unitOn W (ψ * φσ)⁻¹) := by
    intro E hE
    have hc : (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).coeff E = 0 := by
      by_contra hne
      obtain ⟨y, hyE, hyW⟩ := hE
      exact hW y hyW (DivisorWithCoeffs.mem_supp_iff.mpr ⟨E, hne, hyE⟩)
    rw [Divisor.zeroDivisor_eq, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_add, coeff_principalDivisor,
      hψ E hE] at hc
    have hc' : E.ord φσ + E.ord ψ = 0 := hc
    refine Or.inr ?_
    change WithZero.exp _ ≤ E.valuation
      ((((ψ * φσ)⁻¹ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) E.component)
    rw [E.valuation_component, PrimeDivisor.ord_inv, PrimeDivisor.ord_mul,
      DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_zero, neg_zero]
    rw [WithZero.exp_le_exp]
    omega
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := Divisor.IsDivisorialSection.exists_eq hinv
  refine IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one t (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf_app_injective W ?_)
  rw [map_mul, map_one, ht]
  funext Z
  change (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (op W) r Z * unitOn W (ψ * φσ)⁻¹ Z = 1
  rw [hr Z]
  change _ * (((ψ * φσ)⁻¹ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ) : RationalFunctions X) Z.1 = 1
  rw [← Pi.mul_apply, ← Units.val_mul, mul_inv_cancel, Units.val_one, Pi.one_apply]

/-- **Off the support of `(σ)₀` the section `σ` does not vanish.** -/
private theorem mem_nonvanishingOpen_of_notMem_supp (hD : D.IsCartier)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X D.divisorialSheaf]
    (σ : D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).supp) :
    x ∈ Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.nonvanishingOpen X D.divisorialSheaf σ := by
  set L := D.divisorialSheaf
  haveI : SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L :=
    (inferInstance : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L)
  set σ' : Γ(L, ⊤) := σ
  have hσ0 : σ' ≠ 0 := hσ
  have hevaltop : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop L σ').eval (Opposite.op ⊤) = σ' :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop_eval_top _ σ'
  have hne0' : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop L σ').eval (Opposite.op ⊤) ≠ 0 := by
    rwa [hevaltop]
  have hcompl := nonvanishingLocus_eq_compl_supportSet_zeroScheme L _ hne0'
  have hnv : Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus L σ' =
      (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X L
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop L σ').eval (Opposite.op ⊤))).supportSetᶜ := by
    rw [← hcompl]
    conv_lhs => rw [← hevaltop]
    rw [← Stacks.AmplePredicateBridge.coe_nonvanishingOpen_eval X _
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsOfTop L σ')]
    rfl
  rw [hevaltop] at hnv
  rw [Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.mem_nonvanishingOpen, hnv]
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, ψ, hψ⟩ := hD x
  let V : X.Opens := U ⊓
    ⟨((D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).supp : Set X)ᶜ, (D.zeroDivisor σ hσ).supp.isClosed.isOpen_compl⟩
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWV⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
    (show x ∈ V from ⟨hxU, hx⟩)
  have hψW := hψ.mono (hWV.trans inf_le_left)
  set r := trivialization hψW (D.divisorialSheaf.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op σ)
  have hideal : (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X L σ').ideal ⟨W, hW⟩ = Ideal.span {r} :=
    zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X L σ' ⟨W, hW⟩ (trivialization hψW) r rfl
  have hu : IsUnit r := isUnit_trivialization_restrict hψW σ hσ fun y hy => (hWV hy).2
  intro hmem
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem (U := ⟨W, hW⟩) hxW, hideal,
    Scheme.zeroLocus_span, Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton] at hmem
  exact hmem (by rwa [X.basicOpen_of_isUnit hu])

end ZeroScheme

section Bertini

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceGeneratingSections (globalSectionsModule) in
attribute [local instance] globalSectionsModule in
/-- **Bertini for the reducedness of a free system of divisorial sections.** For a general
coefficient vector `c`, every coefficient of the divisor of zeros of `∑ᵢ cᵢ sᵢ` is at most `1`. -/
private theorem exists_dense_open_coeff_zeroDivisor_le_one (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNormal X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] (hX : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k f) {D : Divisor X}
    (hD : D.IsCartier) {N : ℕ} (s : Fin (N + 1) → D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤)
    (hfree : ∀ x : X, ∃ (i : Fin (N + 1)) (hi : s i ≠ 0), x ∉ (D.zeroDivisor (s i) hi).supp) :
    ∃ U : (MMP.Threefold.Bridges.coefficientSpace k N).Opens,
      Dense (U : Set (MMP.Threefold.Bridges.coefficientSpace k N)) ∧
      ∀ c : Fin (N + 1) → k, MMP.Threefold.Bridges.coefficientPoint c ∈ U →
        ∀ (hc : ∑ i, scalarsToGlobalSections k f (c i) • s i ≠ 0) (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X),
          (D.zeroDivisor _ hc).coeff E ≤ 1 := by
  letI : X.Over (Spec (.of k)) := ⟨f⟩
  haveI := hD.isInvertibleModule_divisorialSheaf
  haveI : SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property D.divisorialSheaf :=
    (inferInstance : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X D.divisorialSheaf)
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) := hX.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  haveI : QuasiCompact (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) := hX.toQuasiCompact
  let s' : Fin (N + 1) → Γ(D.divisorialSheaf, ⊤) := s
  have hsys : ∀ c : Fin (N + 1) → k, MMP.Threefold.Bridges.systemSection s' c =
      (∑ i, scalarsToGlobalSections k f (c i) • s i : D.divisorialSubmodule ⊤) := fun c => by
    rw [MMP.Threefold.Bridges.systemSection_apply]
    rfl
  have hs : ⨆ c : Fin (N + 1) → k, Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.nonvanishingOpen X D.divisorialSheaf
      (MMP.Threefold.Bridges.systemSection s' c) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => ?_
    obtain ⟨i, hi, hx⟩ := hfree x
    refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨Pi.single i 1, ?_⟩
    have : MMP.Threefold.Bridges.systemSection s' (Pi.single i (1 : k)) = s' i := by
      simp [MMP.Threefold.Bridges.systemSection_apply, Pi.single_apply]
    rw [this]
    exact mem_nonvanishingOpen_of_notMem_supp hD (s i) hi hx
  obtain ⟨⟨U, hU, hUred⟩, -⟩ := MMP.Threefold.Bridges.exists_dense_open_isReduced_zeroScheme s' hs
  refine ⟨U, hU, fun c hc hσ E => ?_⟩
  have hred := hUred c hc
  rw [hsys c] at hred
  exact coeff_zeroDivisor_le_one hD _ hσ hred E

end Bertini

section Assembly

/-- **The cyclic cover of a branched equation is a normal variety.** If `div φ + mM ≥ 0` has
all coefficients at most `1` and some coefficient equal to `1`, the cyclic cover defined by
`(M, m, φ)` over a normal variety in characteristic zero is a normal variety. -/
private theorem isNormalVariety_toBase (k : Type u) [Field k] [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
    (hX : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k f) (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (M : Divisor X)
    {φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ} (hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • M)
    (h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * M.coeff E ≤ 1)
    (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (hE : E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * M.coeff E = 1) :
    MMP.Mori.IsNormalVariety k (toBase m M hφ ≫ f) := by
  have hm : ∀ x : X, IsUnit (m : X.presheaf.stalk x) := fun x => by
    let ψ : k →+* X.presheaf.stalk x :=
      ((X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.comp f.appTop.hom).comp
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv.hom
    have : (m : X.presheaf.stalk x) = ψ (m : k) := by simp
    rw [this]
    exact (IsUnit.mk0 (m : k) (Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (NeZero.ne m))).map ψ
  have hirr := irreducible_poly m M E hE
  haveI := hX
  haveI := isFinite_toBase m M hφ
  haveI := isIntegral_cover m M hφ hm h01 hirr
  exact ⟨{ }, isNormal_cover m M hφ hm h01 hirr⟩

end Assembly

/-- **A general cyclic cover branched along a free linear system is a normal variety.** Let `X`
be a normal variety of dimension at least one over an algebraically closed field `k` of
characteristic zero, `M` a Weil divisor with `mM` Cartier (`m ≥ 1`), and `s₀, …, s_N` global
sections of `𝒪_X(mM)` spanning a basepoint-free linear system whose general member is nonempty.
Then there is a dense open `U` of the coefficient space `𝔸ᴺ⁺¹_k` such that for every `c` with
`[c] ∈ U` the section `σ = ∑ᵢ cᵢ sᵢ` is nonzero and, `φ ∈ K(X)^×` being `σ` read as a rational
function, the cyclic cover `MMP.Mori.DivisorialCyclicCover.toBase m M hφ` defined by `(M, m, φ)`
is a normal variety over `k`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km5d_general_ramified_cover_normal"]
public theorem exists_dense_open_isNormalVariety_cover (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNormal X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] (hX : IsVariety k f)
    (hdim : 1 ≤ topologicalKrullDim X) (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (M : Divisor X)
    (hmM : (m • M).IsCartier) {N : ℕ} (s : Fin (N + 1) → (m • M).divisorialSubmodule ⊤)
    (hfree : ∀ x : X, ∃ (i : Fin (N + 1)) (hi : s i ≠ 0),
      x ∉ ((m • M).zeroDivisor (s i) hi).supp)
    (hne : ∃ U : (coefficientSpace k N).Opens, Dense (U : Set (coefficientSpace k N)) ∧
      ∀ c : Fin (N + 1) → k, coefficientPoint c ∈ U →
        ∃ hc : ∑ i, scalarsToGlobalSections k f (c i) • s i ≠ 0,
          (m • M).zeroDivisor _ hc ≠ 0) :
    ∃ U : (coefficientSpace k N).Opens, Dense (U : Set (coefficientSpace k N)) ∧
      ∀ c : Fin (N + 1) → k, coefficientPoint c ∈ U →
        ∑ i, scalarsToGlobalSections k f (c i) • s i ≠ 0 ∧
        ∀ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ, (φ : RationalFunctions X) =
            Divisor.sectionToRationalFunctions (∑ i, scalarsToGlobalSections k f (c i) • s i) →
          ∃ hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • M, IsNormalVariety k (toBase m M hφ ≫ f) := by
  obtain ⟨UB, hUB, hB⟩ := exists_dense_open_coeff_zeroDivisor_le_one k f hX hmM s hfree
  obtain ⟨U1, hU1, h1⟩ := hne
  refine ⟨U1 ⊓ UB, ?_, fun c hc => ?_⟩
  · rw [Opens.coe_inf]
    exact Dense.inter_of_isOpen_left hU1 hUB U1.isOpen
  obtain ⟨hσ, hZ⟩ := h1 c hc.1
  refine ⟨hσ, fun φ hφeq => ?_⟩
  have hunit : φ = (Divisor.isUnit_sectionToRationalFunctions hσ).unit :=
    Units.ext (hφeq.trans (IsUnit.unit_spec _).symm)
  have hzd : principalDivisor φ + m • M = (m • M).zeroDivisor _ hσ := by
    rw [Divisor.zeroDivisor_eq, hunit]
  have hφ : 0 ≤ principalDivisor φ + m • M := hzd ▸ Divisor.zeroDivisor_nonneg _ _ hσ
  have hcoeff : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X,
      ((m • M).zeroDivisor _ hσ).coeff E = E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * M.coeff E := fun E => by
    rw [← hzd, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_add, coeff_principalDivisor, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_smul,
      nsmul_eq_mul]
  have h01 : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, E.ord φ + (m : ℤ) * M.coeff E ≤ 1 := fun E => by
    rw [← hcoeff]
    exact hB c hc.2 hσ E
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ : ∃ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, ((m • M).zeroDivisor _ hσ).coeff E ≠ 0 := by
    by_contra h
    push Not at h
    exact hZ (Finsupp.ext h)
  have hE0 := Divisor.zeroDivisor_nonneg _ _ hσ E
  refine ⟨hφ, isNormalVariety_toBase k f hX m M hφ h01 E ?_⟩
  have := h01 E
  rw [← hcoeff] at this ⊢
  change 0 ≤ ((m • M).zeroDivisor _ hσ).coeff E at hE0
  omega

end CyclicCover

end MMP.Mori.DivisorialCyclicCover

